\par\par \b \uc2 S$ Rises as It Asserts Its Status as Safe-Haven  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2014\par 04:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0236 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] In another sign of risk aversion, the Singapore dollar--considered a regional safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --is gaining while its neighbors such as the Malaysia ringgit and the Indonesia rupiah decline. The fall of USD/SGD Friday bucks the trend of the broadly stronger greenback. While most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are weaker following the sharp selloff on Wall Street overnight, the Singapore dollar is stronger at 1.2702 versus its Thursday close of 1.2714. The USD/SGD slipped past its 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 1.2706 and has dipped below the round-figure trading barrier of 1.2700. A daily close below 1.2658 would activate the Bollinger downtrend channel that forecasts more Singapore dollar strength versus the U.S. dollar in the near term. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0224 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The slowdown in the Philippines' September inflation to 4.4%--after rising at an annual pace of 4.9% in both July and August--reduces the possibility the \uc2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas\uc2  will tighten monetary policy, says \uc2 ING\uc2  regional economist \uc2 Tim Condon\uc2 . So far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised rates on reverse repurchase agreements and special deposit accounts, and has increased banks' reserve requirement ratio. "However, we think the threat of BSP tightening decreases the attractiveness of peso-denominated financial assets, which will limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's clawback of September's 3.06% depreciation in what we think will be a risk-on October," says Condon. USD/PHP settled Thursday at 44.625 and opened trading Friday at 44.77. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/IDR is higher at 12,210 vs 12,190 late Thursday as the Wall Street's heavy losses overnight is dampening risk appetite. "There's been no indication of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far, but they may start selling dollars if the greenback rises above IDR12,250," a dealer says. Dealers suspected the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday when the local unit fell to an eight-month low on combination of dollar's strength and concerns over domestic politics. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered\f28 \uc2 \f2  now forecasts the USD/IDR to close the year at 12,200 vs its previous forecast of 11,600. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0219 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/PHP has rebounded away from the 20-day Bollinger mid support line at 44.50--also a psychological trading barrier--and is heading for the uptrend channel at 44.86. The U.S. dollar index bounced overnight despite another drop in the benchmark 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield. The conflicting signals for the U.S. dollar suggest USD/PHP may continue to lack directional momentum--unless it ends the day inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. Confirmation of the uptrend channel coming into effect could lead USD/PHP to 45.17 in the near term. The peso is wilting under pressure as investors seemingly dump stocks and other higher-yielding investments for safe haven assets such as the U.S. dollar and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds. USD/PHP is now 44.74 from its Thursday close of 44.63. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ALP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0218 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Australian shares are sharply weaker in the wake of losses on Wall Street overnight amid renewed worries about the pace of global economic growth. The second-sharpest fall of the year-to-date saw the S&P/ASX 200 hit an eight-month intraday low as growth concerns continue to weigh on oil prices and energy stocks in particular. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woodside Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  (WPL.AU) is down 2.4% and smaller Santos (STO) is 2.6% lower. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RIO.AU) is 2.6% weaker and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BHP.AU) is trading at a 15-month low, down 2.2%. "The local market is taking last night's tumble in the U.S. seriously," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  market analyst Steven Daghlian, adding that by lunchtime 997.7 million shares had been traded, worth A$2.36 billion. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASX\f28 \uc2 \f2  200 is down 1.6% at 5210.8. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0215 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malcolm Edey\f28 \uc2 \f2 , an assistant governor of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , says the Australian government's budget that mixed spending cuts with tax rises isn't influencing the setting of interest rates. "It isn't causing a serious problem," Edey says at a conference in Sydney. Treasurer Joe Hockey announced in May a plan to restore the budget to surplus by the end of the decade. A criticism of some economists at the time was that the budget would further weaken already tepid growth. (james.glynn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0212 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Three of China's top four state banks have eased mortgage lending in accordance with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's latest rules. The three banks--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Industrial & Commercial Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1398.HK), \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Construction Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (0939.HK) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  (3988.HK)--have pledged to offer homebuyers with no mortgage debt to purchase a second home at the attractive terms typically offered to first-time buyers. \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in the new rules last week that buyers who own one home and paid off their mortgages could be considered first-home buyers, meaning that they would be eligible for as low as 30% down payments compared with 60% ratio previously. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also allow banks to offer as much as a 30% discount on benchmark mortgage rates. The move is expected to boost demand from first-home buyers and upgraders, but is unlikely to reverse the property downturn, analysts say. (grace.zhu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0157 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/KRW reopened lower after a one-day break over which the U.S. dollar index slipped, but is now rising as the overnight slump of U.S. stocks triggered broad risk aversion. There might be more upside potential for the greenback if the USD/KRW Bollinger uptrend channel remains in play on a Friday close above 1,063. Risk appetite is poor following the 2.0% drop for DJIA overnight - South Korea's benchmark equity index is down 1.2% while other Asian equities are also in the red. The weakness of stocks - which is a negative factor for the won - may however be mitigated by strength in the Japanese yen. The won has a correlation to the yen because their relative values affect the export competitiveness between the two countries. USD/KRW is now 1,072.0 from its Wednesday close of 1,074.1. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0155 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/IDR's bullish technical bias is likely to remain following the overnight rally of the U.S. dollar index. The USD-bulls may be motivated to buy USD/IDR especially since the technical support of the Bollinger uptrend channel appears to be robust at 12,180 - the dollar closed Thursday above this mark despite an initial dip. The 2.0% fall for the DJIA overnight has raised investor anxiety and could lead to liquidation of high-yielding risky assets such as the Indonesia rupiah. This could push USD/IDR toward the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 12,300. On the domestic front, political sparring has analysts concerned that economic reforms pursued by incoming president Joko Widodo may be delayed. USD/IDR is now 12,210 from its Thursday close of 12,180. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0154 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nikkei\f28 \uc2 \f2  is down 1.2% at 15299.25 as overnight Wall St. shares tumbled with the DJIA absorbing a 300-plus point loss. The dollar is also starting to fade, now at Y107.71 after closing at Y107.85 Thursday. "October is historically a volatile month for U.S. equities, and Japan is never immune to the gyrations," says Norihiro Fujito, senior investment strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities, noting that out of some Y2.5 trillion in long stock and futures positions created between mid-August and end-September, only about Y1 trillion worth have been liquidated thus far. "A lot more selling is on the way. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  is almost certainly buying on the dip to forestall a steeper market selloff--as it has in recent days--but this may only spread out the slide over a longer time frame. The body blow will come if macro-economic fundamentals turn sufficiently negative to cause a massive U.S. selloff and dollar collapse. There will be little the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can do to hold the market up in such a scenario." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: CNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0135 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] While the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  will welcome news of a very modest reprieve in investor finance activity in August, recent commentary by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suggests that the underlying strength in this segment of the market, especially in Sydney and Melbourne, remains an area of some concern, says Phil O'Donaghue, senior economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . How investor finance activity evolves over the rest of 2014 will be critical for policy makers. (james.glynn@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0126 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] An assistant governor at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malcolm Edey\f28 \uc2 \f2 , says additional regulatory measures aimed at slowing investor lending for housing will be drawn from "conventional regulation," adding nothing will be created to deal with the problem. Edey says there is some concentration of risk in parts of the housing market, but dealing with it will mean "continuity" of processes already in place. Edey is speaking at a conference in Sydney. (james.glynn@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 09, 2014 22:36 ET (02:36 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141010eaaa0008o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
