\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's c.bank sits tight, keeps key interest rate on hold\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2014\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Policy rate kept at 7.50 pct, where it's been since Nov\par \par \uc2 * Other rates also remain unchanged\par \par \uc2 * Tuesday meeting was last before Widodo becomes president\par \par \uc2 * Current rate 'adequate' for economic goals - c.bank\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Nilufar Rizki\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 7 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday held its key interest rate steady, as widely expected, at its last policy meeting before Joko Widodo becomes president on Oct. 20.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  (BI) said the current benchmark rate - which has held since November 2013 - is "adequate" for keeping inflation within the target and for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effort to rein in the current account deficit, which topped 4 percent of gross domestic product in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 All 16 analysts in a Reuters poll had projected no change to the benchmark rate.\par \par \uc2 Also on Tuesday, BI held its overnight deposit facility rate, known as Fasbi, at 5.75 percent and the lending facility rate at 7.50 percent.\par \par \uc2 For BI, there's no need to raise rates at present, and no room to cut them, especially ahead of next year's anticipated increase in U.S. interest rates. Indonesia, with its large current account deficit, is vulnerable to capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 "We believe concerns about the current account will continue to outweigh worries about slowing growth," said Gareth Leather, Asia economist of Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 HOLD THE REST OF 2014?\par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect rates to be kept on hold for the rest of 2014, unless Widodo quickly raises domestic fuel prices, which would push up the inflation rate. In mid-2013, after fuel prices were hiked, inflation spiked to nearly 10 percent but it has been contained this year.\par \par \uc2 In September, annual headline inflation was 4.53 percent, in the middle of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3.5-5.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's rate hold came at a time the rupiah has been weak. On Monday, it closed at 12,209 to the dollar, its lowest closing since February. On Tuesday, it was trading around 12,200.\par \par \uc2 BI said the rupiah "depreciated slightly during September 2014 in line with U.S. dollar appreciation, which placed pressures on nearly all global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been under pressure in the last two weeks from a strong dollar and also from political developments in Indonesia that have hurt the position of Widodo.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the president-elect scrapped direct elections for regional posts and secured the position of speaker in the new parliament. Widido lacks a majority in the newly sworn-in legislature, which could thwart his efforts to carry out reforms.\par \par \uc2 In a joint press conference by the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Agus Martowardojo said BI is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to the stabilise rupiah in what he called a "healthy" range.\par \par \uc2 PRESSURE ON WIDODO\par \par \uc2 The bank also recently said it is willing to step into the secondary market for sovereign bonds to stabilise the yield in case of a spike.\par \par \uc2 The weaker rupiah could mean ballooning fuel subsidies in the state budget, as Indonesia is sizable importer of refined oil.\par \par \uc2 That can add to pressure for Widodo to raise domestic fuel prices - by cutting subsidies - to contain the budget deficit for this year. However, Finance Minister Chatib Basri said on Monday that the budget deficit is still manageable.\par \par \uc2 Widodo has pledged to phase out fuel subsidies during his term to free up budget funds for infrastructure, agriculture, healthcare and education. He hasn't been clear on when he will start cutting subsidies.\par \par \uc2 Juniman, economist with BII bank, said if fuel prices rise by 3,000 rupiah (US 25 cents) a litre, "inevitably BI will have to raise the policy rate."\par \par \uc2 A higher policy rate will hurt economic growth, which in April-June was at its slowest pace since 2009. BI has forecast annual growth of 5.02 percent in the third quarter. (1 US dollar = 12,200.0000 rupiah) (Additional reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-7T12:25:46.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141007eaa700at0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
