\par\par \b \uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  to Stabilize USD/IDR -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2014\par 05:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0302 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  said it sold dollars in the market last month to stabilize the rupiah's exchange rate, citing the move as one of the reasons for the drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $111.2 billion at the end of September from $111.16 billion at the end of August. Dealers suspects \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  mostly in the third and fourth weeks of September when the USD/IDR climbed above 12,200. "We hadn't seen any sign of \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Friday, indicating that it doesn't try to drive the pair to certain level, but only to reduce the fluctuation," a dealer says. They add the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely continue its policy not to defend the pair at any certain level but let the market find an equilibrium for the pair. A weaker rupiah is also needed to help Indonesian exports more competitive while also discourage imports.(i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 06, 2014 23:02 ET (03:02 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141007eaa70007s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
