\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 's cbank says ready for 'measured  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ' in rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2014\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , traders' comments)\par \par \uc2 By Fransiska Nangoy and Adriana Nina Kusuma\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Oct 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to carry out "measured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to keep the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a range it is comfortable with, Governor Agus Martowardojo said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 He also emphasized that the recent weakening of the rupiah against the dollar was in line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His comments came at a joint press briefing by \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 , Finance Minister Chatib Basri and Indonesia's financial services authority (OJK), and came alongside the release of the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 's twice-yearly regional report that highlighted risks to the country from capital flight.\par \par \uc2 Chatib said the rupiah has weakened mainly because of the strengthening of the dollar. He acknowledged that domestic sentiment has affected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, but said the impact of political conditions on rupiah trading is short-term.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has fallen 4 percent against the dollar in the past three months, while the stock index has declined by 3.7 percent since the end of August, mainly on doubts over President-elect Joko Widodo's ability to foster reforms owing to tough opposition in the parliament, where his coalition has a minority of seats.\par \par \uc2 Losses for the rupiah and shares also been driven in part by worries over Indonesia's vulnerability to the rise in U.S. interest rates next year, because of how dependent the country is on foreign capital to fund its current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, a Bank Indonesia deputy governor also said \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy bonds from the secondary market if the yield spiked too high in a short time. However, traders in Jakarta has not seen signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market so far.\par \par \uc2 "BI rarely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market, but I think they want investors to know that they are ready to support the bond market," a trader said.\par \par \uc2 WORLD BANK\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Bank\uc2 's report released on Monday estimated that Indonesia's growth, owing to its reliance on exporting commodities, will drop to 5.2 percent this year from 5.8 percent in 2013. In April, it projected 2014 growth of 5.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The bank highlighted Indonesia's vulnerability to a reversal of capital flows.\par \par \uc2 "Across the region, vulnerabilities to capital-flow reversals have broadly declined over the last year; Indonesia, however, remains relatively exposed, owing to its high short-term external financing needs," the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The report spoke of how unwinding of half a decade of global easy monetary policies could result in abrupt market reactions, increased volatility, and raise the risk of disorderly exchange rate and interest-rate movements.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Bank\uc2  said Indonesia's projected 2014 current account deficit and short-term debt together amount to a relatively large 10 percent of GDP and 77 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and that external financing relied heavily on portfolio inflows, which had reached record levels in 2014.\par \par \uc2 "These inflows include both foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt and local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt held by overseas investors, generating significant exchange-rate and rollover risk," the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  said. (Additional reporting by Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-6T09:17:44.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141006eaa60069a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
