\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Surges on Hint of Faster U.S. Rate Hikes -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2014\par 03:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1429-6.1497    6.1361-6.1565 \par USD/TWD   30.090-30.360    30.000-30.500 \par USD/KRW    1,040-1,050      1,031-1,060 \par USD/SGD   1.2631-1.2700    1.2600-1.2800 \par USD/MYR   3.2200-3.2360    3.2090-3.2500 \par USD/THB    32.22-32.32      32.07-32.51 \par USD/PHP    44.20-44.50      44.00-45.00 \par USD/IDR   11,850-12,000    11,800-12,105 \par USD/INR    61.00-61.50      60.85-61.74 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--possible uptrend. USD/CNY may rebound if the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  adjusts the daily USD/CNY benchmark rate higher in line with the sharp rise of the U.S. dollar index overnight. Spot USD/CNY might re-enter the daily Bollinger uptrend channel on a Thursday close above 6.1496 and thus adopt a bullish technical bias. The risk-positive effect of the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's newly announced 500 billion yuan lending facility may have faded as some analysts dismissed it as a funding stability tool rather than an economic stimulus. The greenback rallied sharply after the U.S. Federal Reserve concluded its FOMC meeting. Though there were no surprises in the language used by the \uc2 Fed\uc2  to describe its view on interest rates, a forecast of interest rates a year from now suggested that the committee expects a quicker pace of rate increases once the rate-hiking cycle begins. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1429 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 6.1361 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1293 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.1497 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.1500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.1565 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--uptrend. USD/TWD may soon hit its April peak of 30.360 as the greenback surges broadly after the U.S. Federal Reserve FOMC meeting. Though there were no surprises in the language used by the \uc2 Fed\uc2  to describe its view on interest rates, a forecast of interest rates a year from now suggested that the committee expects a quicker pace of rate increases once the rate-hiking cycle begins. In the offshore market, the USD/TWD nondeliverable forward contract is priced at a slight premium to the spot contract price, suggesting a mild bullish bias for the U.S. dollar. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.090 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier), before 29.980 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone and 20-day Bollinger mid line). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.360 (April high), before 30.500 (psychological trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--uptrend. USD/KRW gaps much higher to open at 1,041.3 versus its last close of 1,034.9, representing a 0.6% depreciation of the South Korea won versus the U.S. dollar. The next target for USD/KRW could be the round-figure trading barrier at 1.050. The greenback soared overnight after a U.S. Federal Reserve forecast of interest rates a year from now suggested that the rate-setting committee expects a quicker pace of rate increases once the rate-hiking cycle begins. Traders have recently highlighted the correlation of USD/KRW with regional counterpart USD/JPY as a key factor keeping USD/KRW in a strong uptrend. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,040 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,031 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,050 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,060 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend. USD/SGD rises to a six-month high of 1.2694 as the market reacts to the possibility that the U.S. Federal Reserve is leaning toward a quicker pace rise in U.S. interest rates. The round-figure trading barrier at 1.2700 if breached could trigger stoploss orders that would cause a spike in USD/SGD. Though there were no surprises in the language used by the \uc2 Fed\uc2  to describe when it would raise interest rates, a forecast of interest rates a year from now suggested that the committee now expects a quicker pace of rate increases once the rate-hiking cycle begins. The previous forecast had painted a more gradual trajectory for interest rate hikes. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2631 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2561 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2700 (round-figure trading barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend. USD/MYR jumps to the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, confirming the upward technical bias persists, as the market reacts to the possibility that U.S. interest rates could rise at a quicker-than-expected pace. The highlight of the day is the impending policy decision by \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2 . Analysts are split as to whether the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates by another quarter percentage point as they did in July. Consumer price inflation rose 3.3% on-year according to data published on Wednesday -- above analysts' forecast for a 3.2% increase -- which might make it easier for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to justify an inflation-fighting rate hike. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2200 (psychological support), then at 3.2090 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.2360 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2500 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--uptrend. USD/THB is now above the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, making it likely to keep rising toward the psychological trading barrier at 32.50. The U.S. dollar has surged across the board as the market factors in the possibility that U.S. interest rates could rise at a quicker-than-expected pace. The baht and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all weaker versus the U.S. dollar and could bring a chill to Southeast Asian equity markets. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.22 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 32.19 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.07 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 32.32 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.50 (psychological resistance), before 32.51 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--uptrend. The U.S. Federal Reserve has provided the catalyst for USD/PHP to rally past the 200-day moving average line at 44.20 -- a medium-term technical resistance. The greenback could be on its way to 44.59 where the top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone may stall its advance. The dollar surged overnight after a \uc2 Fed\uc2  forecast of interest rates a year from now showed that the expected pace of rate increases has risen versus the previous forecast. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.20 (200-day moving average), then at 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.93 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.50 (psychological resistance), then at 44.59 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--uptrend. USD/IDR may again try to rally toward the round-figure trading barrier at 12,000 with the momentum of the U.S. dollar's overnight rally. \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to support the rupiah via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market if it weakens excessively due to the triggering of stoploss orders above the 12,000 round-figure trading barrier. The dollar has rallied broadly after the U.S. Federal Reserve's FOMC meeting. Though there was no change in the \uc2 Fed\uc2 's view on when it would raise interest rates, the committee's forecast of interest rates a year from now suggested a quicker pace of rate increases once the rate-hiking cycle begins. The previous forecast had painted a more gradual trajectory for interest rate hikes. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,850 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,800 (psychological support), before 11,790 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel and round-figure trading barrier), before 12,105 (June high).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--uptrend. USD/INR may break through the 61.55 top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and thus take on a bullish medium-term technical bias. The dollar's broad rally -- triggered by the possibility of a faster pace of U.S. rate hikes -- could then gain significant momentum. The rupee and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are suffering as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors trim short-USD positions after the U.S. Federal Reserve revealed its forecast for interest rates a year from now. The committee lifted its forecast for the interest rate at which the \uc2 Fed\uc2  lends to banks versus its previous forecast in June, implying that the benchmark interest rate may be raised at a quicker-than-expected pace. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 60.85 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 60.81 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.50 (psychological resistance), then at 61.55 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 61.74 (August high).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 17 Sep 2014 21:14 ET  USD/Asia Surges on Hint of Faster U.S. Rate Hikes -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 17, 2014 21:14 ET (01:14 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140918ea9i0006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
