\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Falls Past 12,000 to the U.S. Dollar -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2014\par 03:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0148 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/IDR has breached the round-figure trading barrier at 12,000, fuelled by broad U.S. dollar strength arising from risk aversion. Currently at a 4-month low of 12,040 to the greenback, the rupiah may weaken further on stoploss orders being activated. But traders are wary that the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could step in to prevent excessive rupiah depreciation. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was said to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, capping the dollar around the 12,000 level. The charts suggest 12,070--the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--is immediate technical resistance for the U.S. dollar. The USD/IDR is at 12,0420 from Tuesday's close of 11,985. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0147 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The difficulties facing mining services companies amid a broad decline in commodity prices could get worse if financiers take fright at the number of corporate failures in the sector, says Deloitte. Forge Group was among the highest-profile casualties, calling in insolvency specialists and laying off 1,300 workers in February after losing the support of its lenders in the wake of cost overruns and profit warnings on two power projects. Deloitte says financiers may soon start to review the structure of performance guarantee facilities in place with mining services firms. "Cash-backed guarantees may emerge and create working capital pressures," Deloitte says. Its Mining Service Index fell by 2.05 points in 1Q 2014 to 85.62 versus 4Q 2013, underperfoming the top 200 companies listed on Australia's share market. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0117 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Nikkei is down 0.5% at 15295.57 on light volume, following an overnight Wall Street selloff and on the back of a slightly weaker dollar. "Stocks are long overdue for consolidation," says CSLA equity strategist Nicholas Smith. He downplays any link between this and Prime Minister Abe's 'Third Arrow' economic revitalization speech delivered last evening. "Most of what was said had long been factored into the market, including general talk of cutting corporate taxes and boosting public pension fund investment in stocks. What Abe did not mention was detail, for example, on how the 72% of companies that do not pay taxes will be treated to offset the revenue fall, or over what time frame the GPIF (Government Pension Investment Fund) will move into equities. I suppose we'll just have to wait to find out." (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0116 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The final investigative report about the fatal 2013 crash of an \uc2 Asiana Airlines Inc\uc2 . (020560.SE) plane while trying to land at San Francisco international Airport is likely to renew debate about evacuation delays and mistakes by emergency crews. The \uc2 National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  on Tuesday concluded that a controversial, 90-second delay in evacuating the fiery wreck was partly due to the captain's initial order to wait for the arrival of emergency responders. The board also found that the cabin crew's "disorientation and confusion" contributed to the delay. In describing the actions of emergency responders--whose vehicles repeatedly rolled over the body of a victim on the tarmac--the safety board concluded that crews needed more specialized training. Investigators called for more training to help firefighters use certain equipment designed to pierce aircraft fuselages. The \uc2 NTSB\uc2  also urged creation of specific guidance or protocols intended to prevent victims from being inadvertently run over by rescue vehicles. Amid the confusion and turmoil in San Francisco, firefighters failed to check on the condition of the sole victim sprawled on the tarmac. In other accidents, according to the board, there may be many more injured people near the airplane "at risk of being struck or rolled over by a vehicle" during rescue \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (andy.pasztor@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0045 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Gold prices are rangebound in early Asian trading, but rising crude oil prices could provide a floor amid worries about inflation ticking higher--gold is considered a tool to fight inflation. Spot gold prices rose to $1,325.96/oz overnight--its highest since April 15. "The rally in both gold and silver was largely due to speculators closing out short positions rather than stronger physical demand," ANZ says in a report. Dovish comments by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairwoman Janet Yellen about the pace of economic growth last week boosted gold prices above the psychological $1,300/oz level. Escalating violence in Iraq has also helped to support gold prices. Spot gold is at $1,318.77/oz, down 23 cents from its previous close, and silver is at $20.91/oz, down 2 cents. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @ArpanMukherjee)\par \par \uc2 0006 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The diamond market appears to be showing some sparkle. \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  analyst Lyndon Fagan, on a U.S. site visit with \uc2 Rio Tinto PLC\uc2  (RIO), says the Anglo Australian miner expects the market to be in significant deficit for the foreseeable future, which should help drive prices higher. "Rio currently sees diamond demand running at roughly double mined supply," Fagan says in a note. "Little detail was given on how this shortfall is expected to be met, although it would imply material upside to current prices given our belief that stockpiles at \uc2 De Beers\uc2  and Alrosa are relatively modest," he says. The RapNet diamond index for one carat stones is up 1% year to date, according to data provider Rapaport. (rhiannon.hoyle@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @RhiannonHoyle)\par \par \uc2 2257 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  lowers its 12-month target price on Kathmandu (KMD.NZ) to NZ$3.60 from NZ$3.90 after the company says sales through June, and in particular since the start of the company's winter sales promotion, have been significantly below expectations in both Australia and New Zealand. However, it retains its outperform rating as it believes "KMD remains a long-term sustainable growth story." It notes that "certainly KMD has proved in the past it can recover from short-term weather events." The stock is trading at NZ$3.15. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 18:45 EDT - Oversupply in the thermal coal market isn't likely to lift for the foreseeable future, prompting \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  to cut its forecasts for Australian thermal coal sold from the Port of Newcastle. The broker now expects thermal coal ex-Newcastle to average US$76/ton this year, down from a previous estimate of US$80. \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  also thinks thermal coal will average US$80 in 2015, compared to an earlier forecast if US$83. "Recent price declines have been insufficient to generate meaningful supply rationalization, making it extremely difficult to forecast anything but an anaemic recovery for thermal coal," \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  says. Compounding the problems caused by oversupply, electricity generation in China is offering very little in the way of a demand pull for seaborne coal. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\par \par \uc2 17:50 EDT - The Obama administration has quietly granted permission to two companies to begin exporting minimally processed American crude, in the first softening of the US's four-decade ban on shipping domestic oil supplies overseas, according to a WSJ scoop. Traders have been betting the US would eventually allow exports, and that the spread between the US and global benchmarks would converge. Not much doing there yet; spread stands at $8.19. As for shares of the two companies, \uc2 Enterprise Products Partners\uc2  (EPD) shares inactive after-hours and \uc2 Pioneer Natural Resources\uc2  (PXD) up 0.2%. (christian.berthelsen@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 17:36 EDT - An "unexpected bout of risk aversion" has caused short-term damage to AUD/USD and NZD/USD, says \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Imre Speizer. He says initial optimism fueled by some strong US data were reversed later in the session on geopolitical concerns after over Iraq hit nerves. Speizer notes the only thing on the local calendar is \uc2 Australia's RBA\uc2  Deputy Governor Lowe's speech in Melbourne and China's consumer confidence survey. AUD/USD last at 0.9369 from 0.9412 late Tuesday in Sydney. NZD/USD at 0.8676 from 0.8720 late Tuesday in Wellington. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; @lucy_craymer)\par \par \uc2 17:23 EDT - The New Zealand Debt Management Office's plan to issue a new 2027 government bond helps steepen the yield curve, says BNZ strategist Kymberly Martin. The yield on New Zealand 2023 bonds push up 2 bps to 4.46%. Ten-year swap push 4 bps higher to 4.90%. Martin says the increase in interest rate swaps may also have been "assisted by a lull in the recent flurry of Kauri sovereign, supranational and agency issuance." Martin adds the firm continues to see hedging value in 2- to 4-year swaps. "We see current 'fair value' on 2-year swap around 4.40%, some 20 bps above current levels." Five-year swap sits at 4.58%. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; @lucy_craymer)\par \par \uc2 17:05 EDT - NZD/USD is lower as the greenback performs well overnight following upbeat consumer confidence and new home sales report, says ANZ. "The US data trend remains broadly strong, and some USD strength should be expected." ANZ adds, however, that despite the trend, the third reading on 1Q US GDP and May durable goods orders due later in the global day are both expected to remain subdued. Pair is at 0.8673 from 0.8720 late Tuesday in New Zealand. ANZ expects the pair to trade in a short-term range of 0.8660 to 0.8725. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; @lucy_craymer)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2014 21:48 ET (01:48 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140625ea6p0004f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
