\par\par \b \uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Hints at No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2014\par 07:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0516 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  views the current USD/IDR level as good for both exports and imports, suggesting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. "The 11,300-11,800 level is the appropriate level that will provide incentive for both exporters and importers," senior deputy governor Mirza Adityaswara says. USD/IDR is now at 11,790. The pair has been creeping up since last month due to a combination of political uncertainties ahead of next month's presidential election and seasonal dollar demand. But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seldom suspected of selling dollars to curb the pair. (Farida.husna@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0514 GMT [Dow Jones] The bullish technical bias for USD/IDR - a negative indicator for the rupiah - will persist if the dollar manages to stay above 11,800 by the end of the day. Unless this technical floor for the dollar is broken, the rupiah will struggle to recoup from sharp losses - amounting to as much as 4.7% against the U.S. dollar - sustained since May 19. Economists have recently warned on Indonesia's weakening economic fundamentals - which could hurt foreign investors' appeal for Indonesian assets. Last week, the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said there will be no change in its tight policy stance this Thursday. USD/IDR is now 11,800 from its Tuesday close of 11,805. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0509 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says the gain in Malaysia's April industrial production is consistent with the turnaround in exports, which surged 19% on-year in April, and supports the view that economic growth will remain strong in 2014. The house notes that the industrial production indicator points to sustained growth in Malaysia's GDP, for which it recently raised its forecast to 5.7% in 2014 from 5.4% previously; this compares with 2013's 4.2% growth. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  forecasts 2Q GDP at 5.7%. April IP grew 4.2% on-year, propped up by a pickup in mining sector, which cushioned slower growth in electricity generation and manufacturing output. Exports surged . (jason.ng@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0503 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam said Wednesday its borrowing from China is not significant and its economy doesn't rely on Chinese loans. Chinese investors hold only 0.33% of Vietnamese stocks, Finance Minister Dinh Tien Dung said in response to lawmakers' call to reduce Vietnam's reliance on Chinese capital. Tension between Vietnam and China has risen to the highest level in years following the deployment early last month of a Chinese oil rig in contested waters near Vietnam's coast. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0450 GMT [Dow Jones] Hong Kong stocks decline in lockstep with most other markets in Asia as the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  trims global growth expectations, cutting its China forecast for this year from 7.7% to 7.6% - which "will depend on the success of rebalancing efforts." China's reform efforts are having the right effect on growth but their piecemeal approach is harming sentiment, says \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 : "Although a number of important policy actions have been adopted, reform measures have not been rolled out as aggressively as many had hoped," the bank says. However, Goldman expects a turning point has been reached. The Hang Seng Index is down 0.3% at 23238.88, with China Mobile (0941.HK) leading declines on the index. Casino stocks rally as \uc2 Barclays\uc2  and \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  say some companies in the sector look undervalued. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter: @gregorhunter)\par \par \uc2 0439 GMT [Dow Jones] Base metals are trading mixed after the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  overnight cut its global economic growth forecast to 2.8% for the year, compared with a 3.2% forecast in January. The bank says that emerging markets are expected to face headwinds due to an unwillingness to put in place policy changes in many countries. Slower global economic growth could weigh on demand and price outlook for metals. In copper, the market awaits further news on the ongoing probe by Chinese authorities into fraudulent metal financing deals. LME 3-month copper prices have fallen 2.5% since the start of the month as Chinese authorities investigate whether companies used the same copper stocks held in the port of Qingdao as collateral for obtaining multiple loans. LME 3-month copper is at $6,703/ton, up $28, while nickel is at $18,700/ton, down $75 from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com; Twitter: @ArpanMukherjee)\par \par \uc2 0435 GMT [Dow Jones] A bidding war is brewing on \uc2 Aquila Resources (AQA.AU) \uc2 after sources confirmed to the Wall Street Journal that Mineral Resources (MIN.AU) bought at least a 12.1% stake at A$3.75/share, well above the A$3.40/share cash bid from Boasteel and Aurizon (AZJ.AU). Aquila says it welcomes recognition that the value of the company's shares is well in excess of the current bid from Boasteel/Aurizon. Mineral Resources may lack the firepower on its own to purchase Aquila, but it would make sense to have a seat at the table, particularly given its mining services, contracting and processing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Odds are the Baosteel/Aurizon bid will need to be sweetened considerably to get it across the line. MIN last down 2.2% at A$10.14. AQA last up 3.2% at A$3.60. (david.rogers@wsj.com; Twitter: @DavidRogersWSJ)\par \par \uc2 0431 GMT [Dow Jones] Expectations that crude supplies in the U.S. declined in the week to June 6 remains the key fundamental support for prices, Timothy Evans, energy futures specialist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , says in a report. The closely watched survey from the \uc2 Energy Information Administration\uc2  is due at 1030AM EDT. Analysts expect the EIA to report that supplies fell by 1.7 million barrels in the week ended June 6, a Wall Street Journal survey shows. However, if the EIA reports a surprise rise in supplies, the data could "spark" some profit taking. July Nymex crude is at $104.48/bbl, up 13 cents from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com; Twitter: @ArpanMukherjee)\par \par \uc2 0427 GMT [Dow Jones] Chinese government plans to link trading between the Hong Kong and Shanghai stock exchanges have caught the attention of global investors, who will be watching carefully to see whether access to Chinese capital markets is becoming more straightforward, said Chin-Ping Chia, MSCI's head of equity research and managing director for Asia Pacific. "Investors would prefer simpler ways to access the market and a simpler system," he said. "We do believe that there's continuous momentum, and the Hong Kong-Shanghai connection is one prime example of this." However, the mechanism only covers a fraction of Chinese stocks, and does not include the \uc2 Shenzhen Stock Exchange\uc2 , so MSCI will watch how the scheme is expanded over time, he added. MSCI said it would exclude Chinese A-shares from its Emerging Markets Index today after consulting with fund managers. (gregor.hunter@wsj.com; Twitter: @gregorhunter)\par \par \uc2 0421 GMT [Dow Jones] The New Zealand dollar is pushing higher against the USD, the AUD and the EUR ahead of Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision. "It's hard to see the Kiwi going lower given negative deposit rates in Europe while we are hiking," says Tim Kelleher, ASB's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  institutional sales. The market is widely expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift interest rates by 25 bps to 3.25% so the main focus will be on the accompanying statement and any clues about when the next rate increase might come. Kelleher notes the RBNZ in March indicated more aggressive interest rate increases than what the market is now expecting, so if it doesn't change that track the Kiwi will likely gain. If that's the case, the NZD/USD could head to 0.8650 or 0.8710, Kelleher says. The pair is at 0.8548. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; Twitter: @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 0419 GMT [Dow Jones] Spotty hedge-fund performance hasn't stopped investors from ploughing cash into the strategy this year--May marked the fourth straight month of positive inflows of investor cash, according to industry tracker Eurekahedge. It estimates that nearly $60 billion has been added so far this year even as hedge funds globally are sitting on just a 1.9% gain year-to-date. The MSCI World index, by comparison, is up 2.6% through May. (mia.lamar@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0417 GMT [Dow Jones] Palladium prices are poised for a "steep pullback" in the coming weeks on profit-taking once it reaches $860/oz, ANZ says in a report. Spot palladium, which rose 1.4% overnight and has risen around 19% since the start of the year, is at its highest level since February 2011. Wage talks overnight to resolve a five-month old strike in South Africa ended in a deadlock. South Africa produces about 40% of the world's supply of the metal, which is mainly used in automobile exhaust filters. Palladium net long positions, or bets that prices will rise, are at historical highs, ANZ says. Total holdings in palladium ETFs stood just shy of 2.8 million ounces at the end of May, exceeding the annual production of Russia, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. Spot palladium is at $850/oz, down $2 from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com; Twitter: @ArpanMukherjee)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 11, 2014 01:16 ET (05:16 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140611ea6b000kr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
