                             such day is a Relevant Business \par                                            Day) or (ii) if the first day \par                                            (other than a Saturday or a \par                                            Sunday) following the Fixing \par                                            Date is not a Relevant Business \par                                            Day, at or about 11:00 a.m. \par                                            Singapore time on the Fixing \par                                            Date from five banks active \par                                            in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \par                                            \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets (such \par                                            banks, the "Reference Banks") \par                                            as selected by the Calculation \par                                            Agent. \par                                           If five or four quotations are \par                                            provided as requested, the USD/IDR \par                                            reference rate will be the arithmetic \par                                            mean (rounded to the nearest \par                                            whole Rupiah, 0.5 being rounded \par                                            upwards) of the remaining three \par                                            or two such quotations, as the \par                                            case may be, for such rate provided \par                                            by the Reference Banks, after \par                                            disregarding the highest such \par                                            quotation and the lowest such \par                                 