\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won near 6-year high on inflows, rupiah NDFs up as elections start\b0\par\par\uc2 972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2014\par 07:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won jumps on stocks inflows, offshore funds short-covering\par     * S.Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted, but not so strong - traders\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kicks off parliament vote, PDI-P may win\par     * Taiwan dollar near 3-month high on inflows, exporters\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 9 (Reuters) - The South Korean won hit a\par near six-year high on Wednesday thanks to capital inflows,\par leading gains among emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while the\par Indonesian rupiah rose in offshore markets as parliamentary\par elections started.\par     The won rose as much as 1.2 percent to 1,040.1\par per dollar, its strongest since August 2008.\par     Foreign investors extended a buying spree in Seoul's main\par stock market to an 11th consecutive session, purchasing\par a net 2.5 trillion won ($2.4 billion) worth of stocks during the\par period, according to Korea Exchange data. Offshore funds dumped\par dollar holdings to stop losses.\par     South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of\par buying dollars to prevent the won from strengthening past 1,040,\par but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not seen as strong, traders said.\par     Investors had built up short positions in the won on caution\par that the authorities may keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker than 1,050,\par but the finance ministry or the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had not been\par spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     "It is less necessary to keep the won weaker as the\par government is seeking a balanced development in exports and\par domestic consumption," said Jeong My-young, research head at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures in Seoul.\par     South Korean President Park Geun-hye promised to shift\par economic policy away from supporting big exporters towards\par lifting domestic-market-oriented industries and household\par income.\par     Korea Inc. is also now less vulnerable to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rates than in the past as major exporters such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\par Electronics Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par are producing part of their goods outside the country.\par     Big exporters have focused more on expanding overseas\par production bases than local factories. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to build\par its fourth plant in China for about 1 trillion won, a source\par said last month. \par     In 2013, the won rose 1.4 percent thanks to a sustained\par current account surplus and capital inflows, while most emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on worries that the Federal Reserve's\par stimulus reduction may cause fund outflows from the region.\par     The won's outperformance last year boosted caution over\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and some investors took profits in 2014.\par     Some analysts have said that the caution had been excessive,\par given data showing South Korea's exports were still fine and the\par current account remained in surplus.\par     Technically, the won is seen having room to strengthen to\par 1,032, its low in March 2008, analysts said.\par     Still, the won is considered overbought with the 14-day\par dollar/won relative strength index at 28.3, prompting some\par investors to look for chances to book profits. A reading below\par the 30 threshold indicates the dollar has been sold excessively.\par     \par     RUPIAH NDFS\par     The rupiah rose in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par  markets as Indonesians began voting for a new\par parliament. \par     The rupiah's one-month NDFs rose 0.5 percent\par to 11,195 per dollar, the strongest since Nov. 1.\par     The opposition Indonesian Democratic Party-Struggle (PDI-P)\par is likely to dominate in the elections, opinion polls showed.\par     That bolstered the chances of a victory by its popular\par candidate, Jakarta Governor Joko Widodo, widely know as Jokowi,\par in a presidential election. \par     Potential wins by the PDI-P and Jokowi are likely to attract\par more foreign funds, analysts have said.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar rose as much as 0.8 percent to\par 30.030 to the U.S. dollar, its strongest since Jan. 14, tracking\par the won's strength.\par     The island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found more support from inflows from\par foreign financial institutions and as local exporters bought it\par around 30.100 for settlements.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the Taiwan\par dollar weaker than 30.000, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not that\par strong, traders said.\par     That came as U.S. dollar purchases by South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were not very large.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  looks closely at the won's movements\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as the two compete\par in some exports markets such as semiconductors, traders and\par analysts said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       101.96         101.80       -0.16\par   Sing dlr        1.2500         1.2513       +0.10\par   Taiwan dlr      30.080         30.270       +0.63\par   Korean won     1042.10        1052.20       +0.97\par   Baht             32.22          32.33       +0.34\par  *Peso             44.74          44.74       +0.00\par  *Rupiah        11286.00       11286.00       +0.00\par   Rupee            59.99          60.11       +0.20\par   Ringgit         3.2290         3.2410       +0.37\par   Yuan            6.1944         6.1968       +0.04\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       101.96         105.28       +3.25\par   Sing dlr        1.2500         1.2632       +1.06\par   Taiwan dlr      30.080         29.950       -0.43\par   Korean won     1042.10        1055.40       +1.28\par   Baht             32.22          32.86       +1.99\par   Peso             44.74          44.40       -0.76\par   Rupiah        11286.00       12160.00       +7.74\par   Rupee            59.99          61.80       +3.02\par   Ringgit         3.2290         3.2755       +1.44\par   Yuan            6.1944         6.0539       -2.27\par   ($1 = 1,052.35 Won)\par    * Financial markets in Indonesia are closed for parliament\par elections and the Philippine markets are also shut for a\par holiday.\par \par  (Additional reporti