\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Lower as Investor Fear Subsides -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2014\par 02:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.0500-6.0514   6.0406-6.0600 \par USD/TWD         --              - \par USD/KRW     1,070-1,075     1,065-1,080 \par USD/SGD    1.2724-1.2770   1.2700-1.2800 \par USD/MYR    3.3200-3.3240   3.3000-3.3420 \par USD/THB     32.80-32.91     32.50-33.00 \par USD/PHP     45.21-45.45     45.00-45.50 \par USD/IDR    12,060-12,220   12,000-12,278 \par USD/INR     62.45-63.00     62.37-63.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. The USD/CNY exchange rate is likely to rise for a second day in line with the rally in the U.S. dollar index overnight. Wednesday's fixing may be close to the 6.1100 barrier. This could trigger a mild bullish signal on the spot USD/CNY chart and thereby weaken the yuan further in the near term. Spot USD/CNY may lose its previous bearish bias if it ends Wednesday above 6.0514 and thereby out of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be awaiting the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision later in the day about bond-buying reductions. If the Fed reduces more U.S. bond yields and the dollar will spike higher. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.0500 (psychological support), then at 6.0406 (record low), before 6.0342 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0514 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--retreat and consolidation. USD/KRW gaps much lower to start the day at 1,073.6 versus its previous close of 1,081.2 as traders react to the improvement in risk appetite for emerging-market assets following Turkey's interest rate rise overnight to stem weakness in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar has now dropped out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--losing its upwards momentum. USD/KRW may subside over the next few sessions to consolidate near the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1,065.0. The recent losses in the South Korea won were mainly triggered by risk aversion owing to sharp falls in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 --particularly the Argentine peso and the Turkey lira. Therefore, with the rebound of the lira the won is enjoying a reprieve, too. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,070 (psychological support), then at 1,065 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 1,075 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,080 (psychological resistance), before 1,082 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD may consolidate near the technical support at 1.2724 as investor sentiment improves following the emergency interest-rate rise in Turkey. The Singapore dollar--considered a regional safe haven in recent emerging-market selling--may lose some appeal as a result of risk appetite returning. USD/SGD could therefore rise slightly if investors unwind their safe-haven positions that were long the Singapore dollar. If USD/SGD ends the above 1.2770 technical upside bias may return. The catalyst for such a move may be the U.S. Federal Reserve's monetary policy decision due later today. Many market analysts believe the Fed may announce another reduction in bond buying which will lift U.S. bond yields and thereby the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2724 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2677 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2770 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2816 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation lower. The ringgit rallies Wednesday in sync with other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia as investors respond to the sharp recovery of the Turkish lira overnight. USD/MYR has now fallen out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel thus negating the previous bullish dollar bias and may soon head for the trading barrier at 3.3200. \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets today for its interest-rate policy decision. Most analysts expect no change. But the U.S. Federal Reserve meeting later may have more influence on USD/MYR if the Fed announces another reduction in bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3200 (psychological support), then at 3.3000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3240 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3420 (suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level and top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3500 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. Fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the baht well behaved even as emerging-market-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling brews and political protests in Bangkok escalate. The recent stability of the baht in spite of increasing political violence in Bangkok is likely owing to \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to quell investor panic, one trader said. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  is suspected to be capping USD/THB at 33.10-33.15 and has very large offers placed near those levels to prevent the dollar from rising against the baht. This has been deterring speculative attacks on the baht which has been trading in a narrow range of 32.75-33.00 for the past week. Technical upside bias for USD/THB could be reinstated if the dollar climbs back into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now caps at 32.91. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.91 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.00 (psychological resistance), before 33.13 (4-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--retreat. USD/PHP may slide toward 45.00 as international risk appetite for emerging markets improves. Investors heaved a sigh of relief and are likely to return to Asia emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the Turkish lira's rebound on emergency rate rise by \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. Investor panic may have subsided for now--which may allow the peso to recover but traders are still cautious about being short the U.S. dollar as the U.S. Federal Reserve meets later in the day to decide on a further reduction in bond buying. If the Fed announces another reduction U.S. bond yields will rise and lift the U.S. unit as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.21 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 45.00 (psychological support), before 44.90 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.45 (Monday's 3.5-year peak and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation lower. USD/IDR has rejected the bullish technical signal that had appeared Monday as emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stage a global rebound on the back of the Turkish lira rocketing higher after \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced massive interest rate hikes to stem losses for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Investors had been worried that the Indonesia rupiah could be the next target for speculative investors looking to profit from the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rout. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has helped to prevent the rupiah from falling much and has also helped avert investor panic, an onshore trader said. But U.S. dollar upside in the near term cannot be ruled out as the U.S. Federal Reserve meets later in the day to decide on reducing bond buying. If the Fed reduces bond buying U.S. bond yields will rise and lift the U.S. unit as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,060 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 12,000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,220 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,278 (5-year high), before 12,300 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation lower. The rupee may add to its 0.9% rally on Tuesday--triggered by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's surprise rate rise--as investor fears of an emerging-market crisis subside following an emergency rate rise by \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that boosted the lira overnight. The India rupee is likely to benefit from the recovery of the lira because the fall in the rupee versus the U.S. dollar earlier this week was triggered by losses in the Argentine peso and the Turkish lira--both emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that, like the rupee, are high-yielding and have weak balance sheets. But the USD/INR may have limited room to trade much lower owing to technical support levels close by at 62.45 and 62.37. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.45 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 62.37 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 62.02 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.00 (psychological resistance), then at 63.50 (psychological resistance), before 63.70 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 28, 2014 20:00 ET (01:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140129ea1t0004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
