\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah leads Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  slides; offshore funds sell won\b0\par\par\uc2 888 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2014\par 02:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  corp dlr demand hits rupiah; \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits     * Won near 2-month low, offshore funds cover dlr short positions     * Philippine peso eases; c.bank warns of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2    (Adds text, updates prices)     By Jongwoo Cheon     SINGAPORE, Jan 7 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah led declines among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday with South Korea's won hitting a near two-month low as the dollar broadly gained despite disappointing U.S. data.     The rupiah fell on corporate dollar demand. Offshore funds continued to cut bullish positions in the won both against the dollar and the yen.     The Philippine peso eased as December inflation was faster than expected.     The dollar index, which tracks the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , edged up in Asia even though December U.S.\par \par \uc2  services sector data missed expectations.     "We don't need to ride an emotional rollercoaster due to each piece of data," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2  in Seoul.     "It is inevitable for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall against the dollar as the Fed starts tapering. What matters is 'which one would fall more?'" said Park.     The won is experiencing a correction after last year's strong performance, but it is unlikely to underperform Southeast Asian peers, given South Korea's better economic fundamentals, she added.     The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the second-best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a 1.4 percent gain to the dollar, while most regional units saw losses.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell on sustained demand from local companies,\par while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limited its downside,\par traders said.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched in May 2013 in an\par effort to manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,262\par rupiah per dollar, weaker than Monday's 12,230.\par     Investors were keeping an eye on the government's bond\par auction later in the day. The country aims to raise 10 trillion\par rupiah ($821 million) from the debt sale.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     WON\par     The won lost as much as 0.5 percent to 1071.0, its weakest\par since Nov. 13.\par     Net foreign portfolio investment in South Korean markets in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December fell by the sharpest amount in six months, a financial\par regulator's data showed, driven by stock outflows.\par  \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered some of earlier loss as\par exporters took the slide as chances to buy it on dips for\par settlements. Seoul shares also rose with foreign\par investors buying.\par     "The won may weaken again, but it's up to exporters," said a\par foreign bank trader in Singapore, when asked how much the won\par would fall further.\par     "Today, they are seen buying the won when it was around\par 1,070," he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso eased as Philippine annual inflation in December\par picked up slightly to hit its highest since December 2011.\par  \par     Manila shares fell 0.5 percent, while most government\par bond yields rose.\par     Still, investors hesitated to push the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 weaker than the session low of 44.75 per dollar as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief said it is prepared to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. \par     The peso has been stronger than the level since September\par 2010.\par     Once the level is cleared, it may weaken to 45.36, the 50\par percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation between 2008\par and 2013, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar advanced from the previous close, which\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  managed to be weaker through usual last-minute\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Exporters were interested in buying the unit when it was\par weaker than 30.100.\par     The authorities was spotted aggressively selling the\par island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, indicating it wants the Taiwan\par dollar to be weaker, traders said.\par     On Monday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the Taiwan dollar and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 won have lost nearly 1 percent against the greenback in the\par first three sessions of the year, suggesting it wants the Taiwan\par dollar to track the won.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0430 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   