\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -Rupiah hits 5-year trough after Fed trims stimulus\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2013\par 03:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates levels. For earlier story, double click on ) SINGAPORE, Dec 19 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell and the Indonesian rupiah hit a five-year low versus the dollar on Thursday, after the U.S. Federal Reserve announced it would start scaling back its massive monetary stimulus. The rupiah slipped to 12,225 versus the dollar, its lowest level since December 2008, according to Thomson Reuters data. Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell broadly. The Malaysian ringgit, Singapore dollar, the Philippine peso , and the Thai baht all touched their lowest levels in three months. Due to Indonesia's current account deficit, the rupiah has been regarded as the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  most vulnerable to a winding down of the Fed's bond-buying stimulus, which has fuelled inflows to emerging markets. The U.S.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday modestly trimmed the pace of its monthly asset purchases, by $10 billion to $75 billion, and sought to temper the long-awaited move by suggesting its key interest rate would stay at rock bottom even longer than previously promised. Traders said the rupiah came under pressure due to dollar-buying by banks on behalf of their corporate customers.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They added that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell the dollar versus the rupiah.     \par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched in May in an effort to manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 12,191 rupiah per dollar, the weakest for the rupiah since JISDOR's introduction.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par                                                           \par   Change on the day at   0718 GMT                         \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       103.85         104.28       +0.41\par   Sing dlr        1.2631         1.2615       -0.13\par   Taiwan dlr      29.797         29.745       -0.17\par   Korean won     1059.90        1051.30       -0.81\par   Baht             32.37          32.28       -0.28\par   Peso             44.43          44.26       -0.37\par   Rupiah        12215.00       12150.00       -0.53\par   Rupee            62.28          62.09       -0.31\par   Ringgit         3.2750         3.2545       -0.63\par   Yuan            6.0725         6.0718       -0.01\par                                                           \par   Change so far in 2013                                   \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       103.85          86.79      -16.43\par   Sing dlr        1.2631         1.2219       -3.26\par   Taiwan dlr      29.797         29.136       -2.22\par   Korean won     1059.90        1070.60       +1.01\par   Baht             32.37          30.61       -5.44\par   Peso             44.43          41.05       -7.60\par   Rupiah        12215.00        9630.00      -21.16\par   Rupee            62.28          54.99      -11.71\par   Ringgit         3.2750         3.0580       -6.63\par   Yuan            6.0725         6.2303       +2.60\par                       