\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported Before U.S. Fed; Rupee May Rally -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 2,043 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2013\par 01:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia Wednesday: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0703-6.0800   6.0600-6.0802 \par USD/TWD   29.600-29.680   29.570-29.760 \par USD/KRW    1,050-1,053     1,049-1,057 \par USD/SGD   1.2556-1.2574   1.2529-1.2585 \par USD/MYR   3.2500-3.2600   3.2370-3.2750 \par USD/THB    32.02-32.20     32.00-32.37 \par USD/PHP    44.00-44.29     43.90-44.35 \par USD/IDR   12,000-12,150   11,900-12,200 \par USD/INR    61.50-62.00     61.35-62.42 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. USD/CNY may slip Wednesday as the U.S. dollar index fell again--a sign most investors aren't convinced the U.S. Federal Reserve will reduce bond buying after its policy decision meeting Wednesday. The PBOC central parity rate for USD/CNY is hence likely to drift lower toward the record of 6.1100 marked last week. The spot USD/CNY is near the bottom of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel--an indication the dollar is nearing an overextended skew in terms of market positioning and, therefore, gains for the yuan may not be as forthcoming. The U.S. Federal Reserve's policy decision due later Wednesday will likely be the next trigger for general direction of the U.S. dollar but, even if the dollar spikes on a surprise decision to reduce bond buying, the yuan may not be affected as much as other Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  owing to the view China authorities are speeding up financial reforms that will make the yuan more convertible in the future. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0703 (record low), then at 6.0700 (psychological support), then at 6.0691 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0600 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.0800 (psychological resistance), then at 6.0802 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD has been gradually sloping higher--possibly guided by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward weakness for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The USD/TWD has been trading with a very supportive tone near 29.600 this week compared with 29.560 last week. Ahead of the all-important U.S. Federal Reserve meeting later Wednesday the U.S. dollar is expected to remain stable owing to mixed expectations of what the Fed will do. A few analysts think the Fed could decide to cut back on bond buying Wednesday, which could have a bullish impact on the dollar if the cut is significant. If USD/TWD ends the day above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 29.680, it would be also inside the Bollinger uptrend channel and therefore more bullish on the charts. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.600 (psychological support), then at 29.570 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 29.500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.680 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.760 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation lower. USD/KRW is currently capped by the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,053, and could remain biased downwards as long as the dollar closes Wednesday below this level. The dollar is likely to remain stable until the U.S. Federal Reserve announces its decision on the status of its bond-buying program. If the Fed decides to hold off for now, which is the consensus view, the dollar could easily drop to the base of the Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,049. A few analysts are however predicting a modest reduction in the pace of Fed bond-buying, which likely won't affect investors confidence and therefore should keep the dollar steady or slightly weaker. South Korea stocks are marginally higher Wednesday despite a slightly weak closing for U.S. stocks overnight. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,050 (psychological support), then at 1,049 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,040 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,053 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,057 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,060 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--possible upside bias. USD/SGD has been inching higher before the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision on its bond buying program, which is due Wednesday. The USD/SGD is now well inside the Bollinger uptrend channel and on its way toward a clean break of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 1.2574. A Wednesday closing above this level would confirm two bullish technical signals that could propel the greenback even higher, possibly to the weekly uptrend channel that begins at 1.2668. The Fed's decision is the main factor driving USD/SGD at the moment--even the very poor Singapore non-oil export data on Tuesday failed to impact the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  much. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2556 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2529 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2574 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2585 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR gaps above the psychological trading barrier of 3.2500 at its Wednesday opening versus its Tuesday closing of 3.2470, suggesting an urgency to cover positions by those still short the U.S. dollar. Though the consensus is that the U.S. Federal Reserve won't reduce its pace of bond-buying yet, there is an underlying fear that it is a possibility. U.S. inflation data released Tuesday showed inflation is still not a threat--which makes it less pertinent for the Fed to back off from stimulating the economy. The daily chart now looks bullish for USD/MYR, with the dollar above the entire Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also inside the Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 3.2370. The next target for the greenback could be the weekly uptrend channel at 3.2750. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2500 (psychological support), then at 3.2370 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2260 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2600 (psychological resistance), then at 3.2750 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation higher. USD/THB maintains its bullish stance inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and may be getting renewed vigor to trade higher, as suggested by the spike on Tuesday which follows a series of small-bodied candlesticks that indicated consolidation. While the political unrest in Thailand is on the back burner, the immediate focus turns to the U.S. Federal Reserve policy decision due later in the global day. Several regional Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the rupiah and ringgit have been pressured by the possibility of the Fed reducing bond-buying, but the baht is not viewed as being as susceptible to outflows arising from a pullback in monetary stimulus. The baht is likely to remain weak until February when the elections are conducted. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.02 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.00 (psychological support), before 31.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.20 (psychological resistance), then at 32.37 (3-month high), before 32.44 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation with upside bias. While the daily chart suggests an upside bias for USD/PHP, the dollar is more likely to be stable for now as traders reduce bets and sit on the sidelines before Wednesday's decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve as to whether to reduce bond-buying. A decision to reduce bond-buying would lift \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields and thereby boost the greenback as well. The market has recently been trimming short-USD positions as such, but most of the position adjustment would probably have been done already, so there could be less impetus for USD/PHP to rally further. Traders are still wary of foreign outflows that have recently been dragging the stock market lower and weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  owing to repatriation. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.00 (psychological support), then at 43.90 (base of Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.88 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.29 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.35 (3-month high), before 44.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The dollar's routing of the Indonesia rupiah continues after yet another near 5-year record was hit on Tuesday. The rupiah fell as low as 12,150 to the greenback as traders, sensing a lack of willingness by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against rupiah weakness, bought the dollar on a bet that the U.S. Federal Reserve might decide to reduce bond-buying at its policy meeting Wednesday. The rupiah is widely seen as one of the more vulnerable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event the Fed decides to cut back on bond purchases--which could trigger foreign outflows that will further weaken the rupiah. The Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conspicuously absent in the spot market except for recent verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to talk the dollar down. Even the announcement of raising foreign investment limits in certain sectors of the economy, such as airports and railways, did not help the rupiah to recoup losses. The opening up of the infrastructure sector to foreign ownership ought to help attract inflows that could boost the rupiah. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,000 (psychological support), then at 11,900 (psychological support), before 11,890 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,150 (57-month high), then at 12,200 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 17 Dec 2013 19:57 EDT  USD/Asia Supported Before U.S. Fed; Rupee May -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. The rupee may become an outperformer this week as the market prices in the possibility of a rate hike by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 , to combat a sharp jump in inflation last month, that would nullify any dollar-bullishness ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy decision due later in the global day. The November inflation data printed at 7.5% versus expectations for 7.0%, and raises the possibility that the RBI could hike interest rates again, which would make it a third time in four months. The decision by the India \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which coincides with that of the U.S. Federal Reserve, could lift the rupee owing to the more attractive yield that rupee-denominated assets such as bonds would have. The interest rate differential between that of the U.S. dollar and the India rupee would boost demand for the rupee and thereby push USD/INR lower. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.50 (psychological support), before 61.35 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.00 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 62.42 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 62.63 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 17, 2013 19:57 ET (00:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131218e9ci0006s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
