\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Tests 5-Year Low as U.S. Fed Meets -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2013\par 03:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0211 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar's routing of the Indonesia rupiah continues after yet another near five-year record was hit on Tuesday. The rupiah is back at Tuesday's 12,150 low against the greenback as traders, emboldened by a lack of willingness by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against rupiah weakness, bought the dollar on a bet that the U.S. Federal Reserve might decide to reduce bond-buying at its policy meeting today. The rupiah is widely seen as one of the more vulnerable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event the Fed decides to cut back on bond purchases - which could trigger foreign outflows that will further weaken the rupiah. The Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been conspicuously absent in the spot market except for recent verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to talk the dollar down. Even the Monday announcement of raising foreign-investment limits in certain sectors of the economy, such as airports and railways, didn't help the rupiah to recoup losses.\par \par \uc2  USD/IDR is now at 12,150, against Tuesday's closing of 12,110. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 17, 2013 21:11 ET (02:11 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131218e9ci0002k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
