\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Higher as Fed Meeting Approaches -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2013\par 02:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0703-6.0800   6.0600-6.0816 \par USD/TWD   29.560-29.650   29.500-29.740 \par USD/KRW    1,054-1,058     1,051-1,060 \par USD/SGD   1.2551-1.2574   1.2517-1.2600 \par USD/MYR   3.2320-3.2470   3.2280-3.2500 \par USD/THB    32.00-32.20     31.98-32.37 \par USD/PHP    44.00-44.21     43.88-44.35 \par USD/IDR   12,000-12,100   11,900-12,200 \par USD/INR    62.00-62.63     61.50-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The China HSBC Flash Manufacturing PMI for December will be released which, by expectations, will likely be unchanged from the previous reading of 50.8. USD/CNY is likely to remain near the base of its daily Bollinger downtrend channel as the dollar index shifted only slightly overnight. The PBOC is hence likely to keep the yuan central parity rate stable as well. Though the main focus for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week will be the U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting which concludes Wednesday, the yuan may not react very much until a decision is made by the Fed. The continuing view that the authorities are speeding up financial reforms will keep the yuan in demand and therefore help buffer any spikes by the U.S. dollar. The yuan is by far the best performer in Asia this year, up as much as 2.7% when it hit its 2013 peak last Tuesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0703 (record low), then at 6.0700 (psychological support), then at 6.0697 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0600 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.0800 (psychological resistance), then at 6.0816 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to continue trading sideways as the pair lacks momentum on the charts to break either higher or lower. The dollar has been stable, likely due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and thus has deterred speculators from betting on the Taiwan dollar, which reduces its volatility even further. \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the most active in influencing the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the open market, often buying and selling within the same day to maneuver USD/TWD within an acceptable range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be more active this week as volatility rises on fears of a possible U.S. Federal Reserve reduction in bond buying at this Wednesday's Fed policy meeting decision. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.560 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.470 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.650 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.680 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.740 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation higher. USD/KRW starts the day with a biddish tone and is now peeking out of the Bollinger downtrend channel, threatening to end the downward technical bias for the dollar. If USD/KRW ends the day above 1,054, the U.S. unit may continue to rebound toward the 20-day Bollinger mid and then consolidate. The driver for a stronger dollar is the approaching U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting that concludes Wednesday. The Fed could announce a reduction in bond buying that would drive \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields higher and therefore the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,054 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,051 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,058 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,060 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--possible uptrend. USD/SGD is teetering on the edge of the Bollinger uptrend channel which if confirmed would be a bullish signal for the U.S. dollar. The market is still cautious that the U.S. Federal Reserve might reduce bond buying at Wednesday's policy decision meeting and thus traders are reducing dollar shorts, with some even turning slightly long on the greenback. USD/SGD might take on an even more bullish stance if it closes Monday above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that currently places a lid at 1.2574. But if USD/SGD ends Monday below the 1.2551 Bollinger uptrend channel, it could slide back down to the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1.2517 and then consolidate. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2551 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2517 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2574 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2585 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. A bullish technical bias has appeared in USD/MYR now that the dollar has risen above the entire Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and is now also in the Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports the dollar at 3.2320. The U.S. unit has been getting a lift from speculators covering their dollar-shorts ahead of Wednesday's U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting decision. Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are broadly lower before the Fed decision that could result in a reduction of bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2320 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2280 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.2160 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 3.2470 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation higher. USD/THB is well-supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that nearly coincides with the psychological trading support at 32.00. The charts suggest there is a stronger chance of further upside for the greenback, particularly because of the upcoming U.S. Federal Reserve policy decision due Wednesday, which could result in a reduction of bond buying by the Fed. While there has been a toning down of political tensions in Bangkok, after the military rejected the protesters' calls to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the underlying uncertainty is still a burden on the baht, preventing it from regaining. The next target for USD/THB would be the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 32.39, which is just above the 3-month peak of 32.37 notched Dec. 6. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.98 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.20 (psychological resistance), then at 32.37 (3-month high), before 32.39 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. The dollar is expected to stay supported as the market anxiously looks ahead to the Wednesday policy decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve. A decision to reduce bond buying would lift \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields and have a knock-on impact of lifting the U.S. unit as well. The market has been trimming short-USD positions as such, but most of the position adjustment would probably have been done already, so there could be less impetus for USD/PHP to rally further. The technical resistance of the Bollinger uptrend channel ceiling could be another deterrent to dollar bulls. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.00 (psychological support), before 43.88 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.21 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 44.35 (3-month high), before 44.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR could notch a new 5-year high if it exceeds the 12,100 notched on Friday. The view for a stronger dollar and thereby a weaker rupiah will likely persist Monday as speculators still fear a reduction in bond-buying by the U.S. Federal Reserve after its policy meeting which concludes Wednesday. The rupiah is one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  most susceptible to outflows, analysts believe, due to the amount of foreign fund inflows that have entered since the Fed began its policy of quantitative easing. But the Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may balk at an excessively weak rupiah--even if it helps exporters--because it worsens inflation, so \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rupiah's descent. A senior BI official had previously said that the 11,000-11,500 range would be ideal for both exporters and importers. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,000 (psychological support), then at 11,900 (psychological support), before 11,850 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 12,100 (5-year high), then at 12,130 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. USD/INR is likely to range between the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 62.00 and the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel at 62.63, with a possible bias toward the higher end of this range due to broad dollar bullishness. The U.S. dollar is stronger as the U.S. Federal Reserve policy meeting on Wednesday approaches. Traders are slightly bullish on the dollar for now, as some anticipate a small reduction in bond buying by the Fed. The recent euphoria for the rupee following the state election results, where the opposition party won important victories, has since fizzled out as the market focuses on the possibility of the Fed reducing bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.00 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid and Ichimoku Cloud base), then at 61.50 (psychological support), before 61.35 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.63 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 15 Dec 2013 20:01 EDT  USD/Asia Higher as Fed Meeting Approaches -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 15, 2013 20:01 ET (01:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131216e9cg00069\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
