\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mixed; baht rises on short-covering\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2013\par 03:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Previous day's rise in gold, position squaring lift baht * Rupiah eases on onshore dollar demand (Adds text, updates prices) By Masayuki Kitano SINGAPORE, Dec 11 (Reuters) - The Thai baht rose on short-covering on Wednesday, pulling away from a three-month low set last week on concerns over political tensions, while the Indonesian rupiah fell on dollar-buying by onshore players. Moves in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the baht and the Philippine peso getting a respite after a recent selloff, while those like the rupiah and the Indian rupee retreated. Although there is caution that emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come under pressure if the U.S. Federal Reserve were to announce a scaling back of its monetary stimulus at its Dec. 17-18 policy meeting, some market players say a big shock is unlikely. The market already seems to have priced in the impact of the Fed eventually tapering its bond-buying stimulus, said a trader for a Malaysian bank in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2  "Market is long the U.S. dollar because of this and we now see dollar selling to adjust positions," the trader said. While there had been expectations for a big outflow from emerging Asian markets at one point, that doesn't seem to be happening right now, he added.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     THAI BAHT\par     Traders said long liquidation in the dollar gave a lift to\par the baht, which rose as high as around 31.90, from a\par three-month low of 32.34 set last Friday.\par     A Bangkok-based trader said the previous day's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 short-covering rise in gold helped trigger some dollar-selling, adding that the market had been caught long the dollar. The precious metal is popular among Thai investors, and rises in gold prices often prompt some to sell physical gold or futures. Investors might then sell the dollars they gained from such transactions to buy the baht. Other traders said stop-loss dollar selling was triggered at levels below 32.05 and 32.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The Indonesian rupiah fell as low as 12,012,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 nearing a low of 12,035 set last Thursday, the rupiah's weakest level versus the dollar since March 2009, according to Thomson Reuters data. Traders said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell the dollar, which rose on the back of demand from onshore players. One trader said the dollar was likely to remain on the bid against the rupiah going into the month-end, supported by demand from local companies. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR * Thai baht's previous close is from Dec. 9. Thai markets were closed on Dec. 10 for a public holiday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                          \par   Change on the day at   0546 GMT                        \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.74         102.83       +0.09\par   Sing dlr        1.2498         1.2487       -0.09\par   Taiwan dlr      29.565         29.635       +0.24\par   Korean won     1053.00        1052.20       -0.08\par   Baht             32.00          32.12       +0.37\par   Peso             44.19          44.29       +0.23\par   Rupiah        11990.