\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Likely Higher on Mild Risk Aversion -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2013\par 01:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.0950   6.0873-6.0998 \par USD/TWD   29.550-29.640   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,060-1,063     1,058-1,067 \par USD/SGD   1.2538-1.2576   1.2500-1.2598 \par USD/MYR   3.2200-3.2280   3.2000-3.2400 \par USD/THB         -               - \par USD/PHP    43.80-43.88     43.65-43.92 \par USD/IDR   11,800-11,950   11,720-12,000 \par USD/INR    62.08-62.70     62.00-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The PBOC may set the dollar/yuan parity rate close to its previous fixing of 6.1300 as the dollar index remained roughly unchanged overnight. Spot USD/CNY could continue to bob within a narrow range of 6.0900-6.0950, capped by the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone above. The greenback is likely to stay firm before Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls data. The private payrolls report published by ADP on Wednesday beat expectations, which sets the stage for a strong jobs number Friday, which could sway expectations for an earlier start to U.S. Federal Reserve tapering monetary stimulus. Optimism for the yuan will likely carry on as China watchers eye the developments in the Shanghai Free Trade Zone. Authorities announced earlier this week relaxed financial regulations for the FTZ, which is encouraging investors to at least hold on to bets that the Chinese authorities will also speed up broader reforms that could broaden the yuan's usage and therefore its value. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 6.0900 (pyschological support), then at 6.0873 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.0950 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 6.0998 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 6.1000 (pyschological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD may consolidate within a range of 29.550-29.710, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid at 26.560 and capped by the ceiling of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The U.S. dollar will likely remain supported after a string of positive U.S. economic data released overnight including private payrolls data, which all beat expectations, boding well for the U.S. non-farm payrolls report Friday. If USD/TWD ends the day above the Ichimoku Cloud ceiling, chances are the dollar could rally further in the near term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.550 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.470 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.640 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.730 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation higher. USD/KRW is likely to trade with a firm tone after U.S. data released overnight beat expectations. USD/KRW may hover above the 1,060 psychological support and could test the technical resistance looming at 1,063 if risk aversion spreads in Asia due to the fear of an earlier-than-expected reduction of monetary stimulus by the U.S. Federal Reserve. The South Korea's main equity index is down slightly, in line with losses on Wall Street overnight, and could add to bearishness for the won. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 1,060 (psychological support), then at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--mild upside bias. USD/SGD is in the Bollinger uptrend channel again after a slew of forecast-beating U.S. economic data released overnight, which boosted the dollar on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve might decide to reduce monetary stimulus sooner. USD/SGD could next aim for the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 1.2576 as traders -- encouraged by the strong ADP private payrolls report released Wednesday -- buy the greenback in anticipation of an equally upbeat U.S. non-farm payrolls report due Friday. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support at 1.2538 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2500 (psychological support and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2472 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2576 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2598 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation higher. USD/MYR may re-enter the Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 3.2240 and could even surpass the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud at 3.2280, which would lend more bullish bias to the dollar, as traders skew their positions toward being long the dollar after a night of strong U.S. economic data. Private payrolls increased more than expected, new home sales rose, and the U.S. trade balance also improved. If USD/MYR ends Thursday above the Cloud resistance, its next target may be the 3.2500 psychological trading barrier. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2200 (psychological support), then at 3.2070 (20-day Bollinger mid ), before 3.2000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2240 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2280 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.2400 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible bullish signal. USD/PHP could pop above the Ichimoku Cloud ceiling at 43.88 as the U.S. dollar turns firmer after a slew of upbeat U.S. economic data released overnight. The dollar would appear to have more upside potential if it ends Thursday above the Cloud resistance zone, and could then rally further to the psychological trading barrier at 44.00. Ahead of the U.S. non-farm payrolls due Friday, private job creation increased significantly, the ADP report Wednesday showed. This has lifted expectations that Friday's number will be as positive and could therefore bring forward the timing of the U.S. Federal Reserve tapering of quantitative easing. The value of the Philippine peso continues to be driven by expectations of when the U.S. Federal Reserve might reduce monetary stimulus, said the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas governor last Friday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 43.80 (psychological support), then at 43.65 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.88 (top of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 43.92 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation with upside bias. Encouraged by uplifting U.S. economic data overnight, the dollar is likely to stay bullish and USD/IDR may attempt to break the 12,000 psychological barrier, though there is likely to be some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a sharp and sudden move higher. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's senior deputy governor Tuesday said the ideal value for the rupiah, which would help exports but also discourage excessive imports, is between 11,000-11,500. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR at 11,800 (psychological support), then at 11,720 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,950 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,000 (major psychological resistance and possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. Due to strong U.S. economic data released overnight, USD/INR could rise toward the upper side of its current technical range between the 20-day Bollinger mid and the Bollinger uptrend channel, which spans 62.08-62.70. Traders are likely to cover their short-USD positions after the very strong U.S. private payrolls data released Wednesday, which offers a preview of U.S. non-farm payrolls Friday, and brings back fears that the Federal Reserve might reduce quantitative easing earlier. Traders are also wary of being short-USD/INR as the oil importers are back in the market buying dollars in large amounts as the dollar-swap facility created by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  to help provide liquidity comes to an end. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support at 62.08 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.68 (base of Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.70 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), before 63.32 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 04, 2013 19:49 ET (00:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131205e9c50003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
