\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht slips to 12-week low, rupiah outperforms on trade surprise\b0\par\par\uc2 897 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Offshore funds sell baht; \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution cuts losses * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees $50 mln trade surplus in Oct * Philippine peso edges up on remittance inflows (Adds text, updates prices) By Jongwoo Cheon SINGAPORE, Dec 2 (Reuters) - Thailand's baht cratered to a 12-week low on Monday as anti-government protesters vowed to topple Prime Minister \uc2 Yingluck Shinawatra\uc2 , while the Indonesian rupiah outshone emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after posting a surprise trade surplus. The baht earlier lost as much as 0.5 percent to 32.26 per dollar, its weakest since Sept 11, as offshore funds sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid the political turmoil. It recouped some of the losses as traders kept a wary eye over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders in Bangkok, however, said they have not spotted official sales of dollars yet.\par \par \uc2  Thai protesters took to the streets to renew their fight to topple Shinawatra, prompting riot police to fire teargas and stun grenades for a second day outside her fortified office compound to keep them at bay. On Sunday, three people were killed in street clashes in Bangkok. The dollar/baht forward rates jumped with the one-month rate up 43.5 percent to 17.00, indicating more investors are trying to buy dollar forwards. "We may see more capital outflows on escalating political tensions. If the Fed tapering fears emerge again, the outflows may accelerate," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2  in Seoul. . "The issue was initially purely political. But now it may hurt economic growth," Park said, adding the bath may test this year's low of 32.46. In November, foreign investors sold a combined net 84.2 billion baht ($2.62 billion) in Thai stocks and bonds. The growing political tensions saw the baht become the second-worst performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November with a 3.1 percent loss against the dollar, Thomson Reuters data showed. Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced as final \uc2 HSBC\uc2 /Markit Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) showed China's factory activity maintained steady growth momentum in November. Still, the gains were tempered as investors awaited key U.S. economic data including November jobs on Friday for clues on when the Federal Reserve would start scaling back its stimulus. Nonfarm payrolls for November are expected to show an increase of 185,000 jobs last month, down from 204,000 in October, according to a Reuters survey of economists. "If a better number on nonfarm materializes, it may be the catalyst for a higher USD/JPY which adds to the upside in USD/Asia here," said Andy Ji, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Ji said he would sell emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on rallies.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose in both onshore and offshore markets as\par Indonesia reported a trade surplus of $50 million in October,\par led by unexpected growth in exports. \par     Earlier, spot rupiah in the local market gained with the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted selling dollars to support the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and as foreign banks bought the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on dips, traders said. In offshore non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) markets, the rupiah extended gains after the data. The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR) , which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in May as part of a bid to manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 11,946 rupiah per dollar, compared with Friday's 11,977. Jakarta shares rose more than 1 percent, outperforming most regional stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso rose on increasing remittances inflows from\par overseas Filipino workers.\par     "If all other things remain quiet, the inflows may drive\par dollar/peso lower in coming sessions," said a senior Philippine\par bank trader in Manila.\par     The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may strengthen to 43.50 per dollar,\par the trader added.\par     Some traders booked profits as they waited for the key U.S.\par economic indicators.\par     \par    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par    Change on the day at 0440 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       102.34         102.42       +0.08\par   Sing dlr        1.2536         1.2550       +0.11\par   Taiwan dlr      29.565         29.679       +0.39\par   Korean won     1058.10        1058.20       +0.01\par   Baht             32.16          32.11       -0.16\par   Peso             43.71          43.76       +0.11\par   Rupiah        11885.00       11955.00       +0.59\par   Rupee            62.29          62.44       +0.24\par   Ringgit         3.2215         3.2230       +0.05\par   Yuan            6.0927         6.0932       +0.01\par  \par   Change so far in 2013