\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Firmer, but South Korea Bucks Trend -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2013\par 01:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0802-6.1030 \par USD/TWD   29.560-29.650   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,058-1,063     1,053-1,066 \par USD/SGD   1.2519-1.2568   1.2500-1.2598 \par USD/MYR   3.2160-3.2370   3.2000-3.2500 \par USD/THB    32.00-32.20     31.80-32.23 \par USD/PHP    43.61-43.80     43.33-43.88 \par USD/IDR   11,800-12,000   11,650-12,200 \par USD/INR    62.10-62.73     62.00-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The spot USD/CNY market is likely to trade sideways for now, as volatility ebbs in the NDF market as well despite expectations for a stronger yuan benchmark exchange rate towards year-end. China's November official manufacturing PMI released over the weekend printed at 51.4, unchanged from the previous month, and higher than the median 51.0 forecast in a Dow Jones Newswires poll of nine economists, damping any remaining fears that the Chinese economy will suffer a hard landing. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0894 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1030 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible upside bias. Bullish technical momentum could emerge if USD/TWD pops above the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that currently caps at 29.710. But if this resistance level holds, consolidation within the Cloud range of 29.480-29.710 will likely continue. The USD index continues to look firm as USD/JPY propels higher toward the 103.00 psychological barrier; yen weakening has a proxy effect especially on North Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The NDF market is turning more bullish on the greenback, as the benchmark 1-month NDF discount is again reduced, bringing the 1-month NDF contract price nearly up to par with the spot price. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.650 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.560 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 29.500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.740 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW briefly fell into a technical bearish zone in knee jerk reaction to the improvement in the \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing PMI for November, which climbed to 50.4 from the previous month's 50.2. But unless the dollar ends Monday below 1,058 and therefore inside the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, USD/KRW could return to its consolidation zone between 1,058-1,063. A factor that could also keep the won from strengthening too much is the increasing strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus trade rival Japan. The yen/won exchange rate is close to its 5-year low, which might trigger a response from the South Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 The Bank of Korea\uc2 , which keeps a close watch on the yen/won cross exchange rate to ensure the relative price competitiveness of South Korean exports, typically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the USD/KRW spot market when the won is deemed to have appreciated too rapidly. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,066 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel)).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. The USD/SGD uptrend continues this week, with a suggested intraday range of 1.2524-1.2564 defined by the Bollinger uptrend channel. As the dollar stays firm across the majors, the top of the USD/SGD Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 1.2598 is coming into sight. This key resistance level may prove to be a strong obstacle for further greenback strength as it nearly coincides with the psychological trading barrier of 1.2600. The dollar's uptrend has been in effect since Nov. 21, and will remain in play unless USD/SGD ends the day below the Bollinger uptrend channel's base at 1.2524. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2524 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2500 (psychological support), before 1.2485 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1.2564 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2598 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. The ringgit may lose more ground against the dollar this week as the daily chart indicates more dollar upside is likely. The USD/MYR uptrend channel is leading the dollar toward the 3.2370 top of the Ichimoku Cloud, which if breached by day's end would generate a stronger bullish signal for USD/MYR. The dollar has been firm, particularly against Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve might taper its bond-buying program earlier due to improving economic data. The USD/MYR daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which has been supporting the dollar's rally since Nov. 21, will remain in play as long as USD/MYR stays above 3.2210 by the end of the day. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2210 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2200 (psychological barrier), before 3.2000 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 3.2370 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 3.2400 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside potential. The baht gapped lower Monday and may fall even further in reaction to escalation of the mass protests in Bangkok that has resulted in a loss of lives due to violence between protesters of the two camps. USD/THB jumped to as high as 32.26 from Friday's closing of 32.03, implying 0.7% loss for the baht. The baht could soon fall to the next USD/THB technical resistance at 32.48. Over the weekend Thai police resorted to tear gas and Prime Minister Yingluck was forced to evacuate a police compound that had come under siege by the protesters. The Thai stock market is likely to suffer as well once it opens, as investors pull money out of the market for fear of political change arising from the upheaval in Thailand. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.20 (psychological support), then at 32.00 (psychological support), before 31.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.48 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may head higher within the Bollinger uptrend channel that now spans 43.62-43.88, as the dollar trades with a firm tone in Asia. The dollar could take on a stronger bullish bias if it climbs above the daily Ichimoku Cloud ceiling at 43.88. The main driver for USD/PHP is still the expectation that the U.S. Federal Reserve might reduce quantitative easing earlier than expected, said Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas governor. Thus the peso's value still hinges very much on the market's view of when the U.S. Fed will reduce bond-buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.62 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.35 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.88 (top of Ichimoku Cloud and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation with upside bias. Despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the rupiah from falling below 12,000 to the dollar, USD/IDR still looks well-bid on the charts. The dollar's spike to a 4.5-year high of 12,000 on Thursday likely triggered authorities to step into the market and sell U.S. dollars to stem the rupiah's fall. However, the Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is notoriously low on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and is thus perceived as having less 'ammunition' to spare for defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This may be a reason why USD/IDR may continue to climb higher in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The daily USD/IDR chart does however suggest a slight pullback may be due, now that the dollar has extended significantly past the top of the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2), which is a sign that the dollar may be overbought by speculators. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,800 (psychological support), then at 11,670 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (major psychological resistance), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible upside bias. There is a likelihood that USD/INR will firm and possibly rise as oil prices stabilize and more dollar-buying oil importers return to the spot USD/INR market due to the gradual removal of the dollar-swap facility provided by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  for oil-import hedging. Last week, the drop in oil prices was cited as a reason for the rupee's recovery, as it could help improve the current account, but consistent demand for the U.S. dollar from onshore oil importers has been keeping USD/INR supported on dips. USD/INR may take on a bullish technical bias if it ends Monday above 62.73 and therefore inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. The deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of India said last Monday said that a 'big chunk' of oil importers are back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market buying dollars, as the government's scheme to allow them to buy USD directly from the RBI gets gradually removed. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.10 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.81 (base of Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.73 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at\par \par \uc2 1 Dec 2013 19:57 EDT  USD/Asia Firmer, but South Korea Bucks Trend -- -2-\par \par \uc2 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), before 63.36 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 01, 2013 19:57 ET (00:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131202e9c200069\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
