\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia May Pullback Then Consolidate -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 2,026 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2013\par 01:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0802-6.1030 \par USD/TWD   29.560-29.650   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,058-1,063     1,053-1,066 \par USD/SGD   1.2519-1.2568   1.2500-1.2598 \par USD/MYR   3.2160-3.2370   3.2000-3.2500 \par USD/THB    32.00-32.20     31.80-32.23 \par USD/PHP    43.61-43.80     43.33-43.88 \par USD/IDR   11,800-12,000   11,650-12,200 \par USD/INR    62.10-62.73     62.00-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. Likely to be another dull session in the spot USD/CNY market, which has barely budged more than 10 pips the whole week, as the U.S. market holiday Thursday reduced volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The PBOC central parity rate is expected to hover around its recent levels, though the slightly firmer USD index overnight raises the possibility of a higher central parity rate. China's recent unilateral declaration of an air defence zone over disputed islands, which has been tested by the U.S. and Japan, has not affected investors' sentiment much. One of the prevailing short-term trading themes in USD/CNY is for a stronger yuan benchmark exchange rate towards end-December, as the PBOC typically sets the parity rate higher for the yuan at year-end. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0894 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1030 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible upside bias. Bullish technical momentum could emerge if USD/TWD pops above the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that currently caps at 29.710. But if this resistance level holds, consolidation within the Cloud range of 29.480-29.710 will likely continue. The USD index slipped firmed up overnight as USD/JPY inched further past the 102.00 psychological barrier; yen weakening has a proxy effect on North Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The NDF market is turning more bullish on the greenback, as the benchmark 1-month NDF discount again reduced, bringing the 1-month NDF contract price nearly up to par with the spot price. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.560 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.480 (base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.650 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 29.740 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW has slipped back into the well-defined technical range of 1,058-1,063 - a band within which the dollar has been bobbing within for most of the week. After a brief spike Thursday, which ended in a much lower closing, the dollar bulls are likely staying on the sidelines for now. Exporters' repatriation of earnings and equity inflows from foreigners helped the won recover from the two-week low notched yesterday. But traders are keeping a close eye on the USD/JPY, which continues to boost USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by proxy effect. The South Korea won is particular sensitive to the value of the Japanese yen due to the rivalry between the two exporters. Further yen weakness may trigger a response from \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2 , which keeps a close watch on the yen/won cross exchange rate to ensure the relative price competitiveness of South Korean exports. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,066 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1,068 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel)).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. As the USD/SGD uptrend continues, the top of the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone is coming into sight. This key resistance level may prove to be a strong obstacle for further greenback strength as it nearly coincides with the psychological trading barrier of 1.2600. The dollar's uptrend has been in effect since Nov. 21, and will remain in play unless USD/SGD ends Friday below the Bollinger uptrend channel's base at 1.2519. The USD/SGD currently appears to be tracking USD/JPY's sustained rally past the 102.00 psychological barrier; the yen has a proxy effect on most Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially when it makes large movements. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2519 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2500 (psychological support), before 1.2479 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1.2568 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2598 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation with upside bias. The USD/MYR uptrend channel has met technical resistance at the 3.2370 top of the Ichimoku Cloud, which could imply that the dollar may ebb slightly before making another attempt higher. If USD/MYR manages to break through the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud, it would signal much more upside for the dollar. The dollar has been rallying recently on speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve might taper its bond-buying program earlier. The USD/MYR daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which has been supporting the dollar's rally since lat Friday, will remain in play as long as USD/MYR stays above 3.2160 by the end of the day. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2160 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2000 (psychological barrier), before 3.1930 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 3.2370 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--pullback lower. A warning sign of an unsustainable rally has appeared on the USD/THB daily chart. The long-tailed doji candlestick formed on Thursday, which is also above the Bollinger upper band (another sign of over-extension) signals trend exhaustion. Coupled with the steep rally that has taken place over November, traders will likely read this as a sign that the dollar will pullback lower, possibly to the uptrend channel base, which is also the Ichimoku Cloud support, at 31.67. Thailand's Prime Minister survived a no-confidence vote Thursday, which was expected, but investors' concerns over the mass protests may linger. The Thai stock market bounce that followed the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's surprise 25-basis point benchmark interest rate cut on Wednesday fizzled yesterday - an indication that investors are wary. The BOT caught markets off-guard, cutting the benchmark interest rate to 2.25% from 2.50%, citing low inflation as a factor behind the decision. Last week, the National Economic and Social Development Board revised down its full-year growth projection to 3.0% from 3.8%-4.3%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.80 (psychological support), before 31.67 (Ichimoku Cloud support zone and base of Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.20 (psychological resistance), then at 32.23 (Thursday's high), before 32.39 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may range within 43.61-43.87, supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and well-capped by the top of the channel which coincides with the Ichimoku Cloud ceiling - thus creating a stronger technical resistance. The Philippines' third quarter GDP grew at 7.0% versus an average forecast for growth of 7.1%. Some analysts say it should be read in a positive light considering the high base last year and the impact of multiple typhoons in 2013. Traders looking at the broader market theme - that the U.S. economy is adding jobs at a healthy pace, which makes it more likely the Federal Reserve will reduce monetary stimulus - think the U.S. dollar remains firm into year-end. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.61 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.33 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.88 (top of Ichimoku Cloud and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--mild pullback. USD/IDR's spike to 12,000 on Thursday likely triggered authorities to step into the market and sell U.S. dollars to stem the rupiah's fall. The rupiah hit a 4.5-year peak of 12,000 despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the 11,900 level onwards. The Indonesia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is notoriously low on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and thus has less 'ammunition' to spare for defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This may be a reason why USD/IDR generally heads higher even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  concurrently. The daily USD/IDR chart does however suggest a slight pullback may be due, now that the dollar has extended significantly past the top of the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2), which is a sign that the dollar may be overbought by speculators. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,800 (psychological support), then at 11,650 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,000 (major psychological resistance), before 12,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 28 Nov 2013 19:47 EDT  USD/Asia May Pullback Then Consolidate -- Asia -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. USD/INR may be rangebound between 62.10-62.73, trapped by the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the Bollinger uptrend channel. Recent drops in the price of oil has helped the India rupee recover, but technical support for the dollar and broad expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve is still on track to reduce monetary stimulus in months to come is likely to keep USD/INR well-supported. The drop in crude oil prices is seen as a boon to the India economy and helpful in reducing the current account deficit, thus beneficial to the rupee. But consistent demand for the U.S. dollar from onshore oil importers may keep USD/INR supported on dips. The deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of India on Monday said that a 'big chunk' of oil importers are back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market buying dollars, as the government's scheme to allow them to buy USD directly from the RBI gets gradually removed. Recent improvement in the U.S. jobs data has raised the possibility of the Fed tapering quantitative easing as early as next month. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.10 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 62.00 (psychological support), before 61.81 (base of Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.73 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), before 63.36 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 28, 2013 19:47 ET (00:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131129e9bt0006f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
