\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Sinks After U.S. Jobs Data Disappoint -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2013\par 02:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0800-6.1096 \par USD/TWD   29.320-29.500   29.200-29.560 \par USD/KRW    1,050-1,060     1,049-1,065 \par USD/SGD   1.2356-1.2400   1.2300-1.2460 \par USD/MYR   3.1340-3.1560   3.1200-3.1620 \par USD/THB         -               - \par USD/PHP    43.13-43.25     42.80-43.50 \par USD/IDR   11,200-11,300   11,000-11,500 \par USD/INR    61.33-62.00     61.00-62.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation with downside bias. The overnight slump in the U.S. dollar could mean the PBOC will set the benchmark dollar/yuan exchange rate lower Wednesday, thereby guiding the yuan toward more strength. A weak September U.S. non-farm payrolls report sank the dollar index overnight, though USD/JPY, which rose as a result of risk appetite returning, could mitigate USD/CNY weakness. USD/CNY could therefore stabilize as well. The market expects more gradual yuan appreciation to come as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lately been allowing the yuan to strengthen in the open market--which will help China to shift its economy toward a more consumption-based one. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1096 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation with downside bias. USD/TWD may slide back down and make another attempt at closing within the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 29.320--which would increase the bearish pressure on the dollar. The dollar took a beating overnight after much-worse-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls data. The technical downside bias for USD/TWD on the daily chart will likely remain in play as long as the greenback remains under 29.560. The drop in number of jobs added in the U.S. last month may add to assurance that the Federal Reserve will be comfortable keeping monetary easing going at its current pace. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.320 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.200 (psychological support), before 29.000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.500 (psychological resistance), then at 29.560 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--downside bias. USD/KRW crashes through the 1,060 psychological support and gaps lower to open Wednesday at 1,057.5 versus its last closing of 1,060.8 after a worse-than-expected U.S. jobs report. The broad wave of dollar selling, on increased expectation that the U.S. Federal Reserve will maintain its pace of monetary easing, is likely to keep pushing USD/KRW lower. The dollar is already at a 9-month low against the South Korea won. Foreign investors' inflows into equities and fixed income assets that have recently been driving won gains will likely resume with renewed vigor now that confidence is brimming that U.S. monetary stimulus will continue. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,054 (9-month low), then at 1,050 (psychological support), before 1,049 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (psychological resistance), then at 1,065 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,070 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation lower. USD/SGD slumped overnight after a disappointing U.S. non-farm payrolls report, and fell sharply back to the bottom of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, which ought to support the dollar for now. There was a flurry of dollar-selling after fewer-than-expected jobs were added in the U.S. economy in September, hence reassuring the market that the Federal Reserve will likely delay tapering quantitative easing--which has a side effect of weakening the greenback. A bearish technical signal will be confirmed on the weekly chart if USD/SGD ends Friday below 1.2380 and therefore under the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and also within the Bollinger downtrend channel. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2356 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2343 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2300 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2380 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2400 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2460 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. As the U.S. dollar weakens across the board after a worse-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls report, USD/MYR still has some way to go before hitting bottom. The base of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 3.1340 now beckons, though the move may lack momentum and could easily bounce on profit-taking as traders try to keep positioning lean ahead of the Malaysia government's 2014 budget announcement this Friday. Analysts and punters will be looking for the government to address the years-long fiscal deficit and the heavy reliance on foreign debt--issues that led to ratings agencies warning on Malaysia's sovereign credit rating. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.1340 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1200 (psychological support), before 3.1035 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.1560 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1620 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.1800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP will likely gap lower and re-enter the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, which will lend a bearish tone to the dollar. Adding to downward pressure is the likelihood of increased remittances as the year-end approaches, when millions of overseas workers remit larger-than-usual amounts to their families before the holidays. The extra demand for the peso could further boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.13 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.80 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.25 (200-week moving average), before 43.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR will come under downwards pressure as regional peers collapse overnight after a disappointing U.S. non-farms payroll report. The dollar sank broadly, sending regional pairs such as USD/MYR and USD/SGD to back toward multi-month lows. However, traders are slightly wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem rupiah strength, in order to keep the country's exports attractively priced. The market will probably choose to express their bearish view on the dollar through the NDF market, which is unfettered by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rupiah is priced much stronger in the pure offshore market, trading at around 10,850 for the 1-month contract versus the official spot market rate of 11,300 - due to hedge funds unwinding bets against the rupiah in recent weeks. Indonesia's fundamentals, though shaky, are improving somewhat, helped by a cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that makes its exports more attractive, hence narrowing the trade gap. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,200 (psychological support), then at 11,180 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 11,000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,300 (psychological resistance), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,530 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. After a dismal U.S. jobs report, USD/INR will likely gap lower on increased conviction that the U.S. Federal Reserve will keep up its pace of bond-buying, thus keeping up pressure on the dollar. USD/INR may break past the 61.33 entrance of the downtrend channel, thus taking on a downside bias for the dollar. The improvement in risk appetite, which sent U.S. stocks to all-time highs, will help fuel demand for high-risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the rupee. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.33 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 61.00 (psychological support), before 60.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.00 (psychological resistance), then at 62.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 22, 2013 20:46 ET (00:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131023e9an0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
