\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Likely Weighed by Positive Risk Sentiment -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2013\par 02:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0800-6.1125 \par USD/TWD   29.320-29.500   29.200-29.580 \par USD/KRW    1,060-1,067     1,056-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2380-1.2400   1.2369-1.2423 \par USD/MYR   3.1500-3.1670   3.1400-3.1800 \par USD/THB    31.00-31.14     30.80-31.20 \par USD/PHP    43.00-43.15     42.64-43.25 \par USD/IDR   11,200-11,400   11,150-11,500 \par USD/INR    61.00-61.29     60.50-61.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--downside bias. As risk appetite remains buoyant, the dollar is likely to stay soft. The increased likelihood of another record low for the USD/CNY daily benchmark rate will keep the spot market trading with a downward bias. The yuan hit a new high of 6.0915 against the U.S. dollar in the spot market Friday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been allowing more yuan gains over the last two weeks; this pattern is expected to continue as China attempts to shift its economy toward a more consumption-based one. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1125 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. The dollar is expected to keep grinding lower, though propped up along the way by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing the descent. The USD/TWD pair has so far stayed resilient ahead of the technical support at 29.320, which is where the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel begins, but this floor may soon break as the dollar is likely to be sold on improving risk sentiment. A growing belief that the Federal Reserve will hold back from withdrawing monetary stimulus anytime soon has been weighing on the greenback and lifting the Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.320 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.200 (psychological support), before 29.000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.500 (psychological resistance), then at 29.580 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.590 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with downside bias. USD/KRW remains heavy on expectations of easy monetary policy from the U.S. Federal Reserve, but the market is wary of Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping won strength at bay. The dollar appears to be well-supported at the 1,060 base of the Bollinger downtrend channel, which is also a psychological support that the BOK might be defending. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps away from propping the dollar up, there could be slippage toward the base of the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,056. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,060 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological support), before 1,056 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,067 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance), before 1,072 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--downside bias. USD/SGD will be aiming to break the base of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2380, which could begin another wave of dollar-selling due to the bearish technical signal. The next target for the USD/SGD pair could be the 5-month low of 1.2261 touched in May. The greenback is likely to stay weighted as the market prices in the reduced likelihood of the U.S. Federal Reserve trimming its pace of monetary easing. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2380 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1.2369 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2300 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2400 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2423 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2477 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. USD/MYR is likely to stay on course for the major psychological support at 3.1000, as the dollar continues to trend lower within the downwards Bollinger channel that now caps at 3.1670. Overall investor optimism stemming from the passing of the U.S. debt ceiling deal and a dovish U.S. Federal Reserve is helping the high-yielding Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to perform. The Malaysia government will release its budget statement this Friday, which could help the ringgit to gain further if the issues of the country's excessive fiscal spending and heavy reliance on foreign debt are addressed. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.1500 (psychological support), then at 3.1400 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.1035 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 3.1670 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--downside bias. USD/THB may head lower within the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that came into play since Wednesday and now places a lid at 31.14. The dollar has a soft tone in general due to improving risk appetite, which is encouraging investors' demand for higher-yielding Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/THB is on track toward the base of the channel at 30.74. The broad wave of dollar selling is expected to continue as expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to taper quantitative easing diminish with the dovish Janet Yellen at the helm. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.00 (psychological support), then at 30.80 (psychological support), before 30.74 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 31.14 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 31.20 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP remains under the bearish influence of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that now caps at 43.15, and could attempt to break the 43.00 psychological support soon. The perception of a dovish U.S. Federal Reserve seems the be the main driver for dollar weakness. Additional pressure on the dollar also comes from the remittance season in the Philippines as overseas workers remit larger-than-usual amounts to their families ahead of the year-end holidays. A break of the 43.00 psychological support, a level not tested since June, is expected to trigger more selling of the dollar due to stoploss orders. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.64 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.15 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.25 (200-week moving average), before 43.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--mild downside bias. The rupiah has been stable recently despite broad dollar weakness, due to onshore demand for dollars, said a trader. But the increasing pressure on the greenback in the region will anchor the USD/IDR lower, possibly toward the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 11,150. Traders are slightly wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem rupiah strength, in order to keep the country's exports attractively priced. The rupiah is still the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia this year, down 15.1% to date, mainly due to current account woes and weakening export performance affecting the trade balance as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,200 (psychological support), then at 11,150 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 11,000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,400 (psychological resistance), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,530 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR has entered the Bollinger downtrend channel, though just barely, thus the bearish signal for the pair is slightly weak. A convincingly lower daily close beneath the 61.29 entrance of the downtrend channel could open the way toward the major psychological support at 60.00. Broad dollar weakness is still the main theme this week, as the market is confident that the U.S. Federal Reserve will keep monetary stimulus going at its current pace for an extended period. There is also growing optimism that India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking the right steps toward reforming the economy, with a proposal to open the banking sector to foreign banks. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.00 (psychological support), then at 61.50 (psychological support), before 60.00 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.29 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 61.50 (psychological resistance), before 62.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 20, 2013 20:36 ET (00:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131021e9al00061\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
