\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Sinks on Fed Outlook, China GDP Data Awaited -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2013\par 02:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0800-6.1138 \par USD/TWD   29.320-29.500   29.200-29.580 \par USD/KRW    1,060-1,068     1,057-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2384-1.2400   1.2300-1.2433 \par USD/MYR   3.1200-3.1470   3.1035-3.1500 \par USD/THB    30.80-31.00     30.74-31.14 \par USD/PHP    43.00-43.17     42.66-43.25 \par USD/IDR   11,200-11,400   11,120-11,500 \par USD/INR    61.00-61.27     60.50-61.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--downside bias. Steep dollar losses overnight, attributed to expectations that the Fed will further delay tapering of quantitative easing, is likely to result in a lower USD/CNY parity rate. The PBOC could trigger more yuan strength if the daily benchmark rate is set at a new record low; the lowest so far was 6.1406 on Monday. The yuan hit a new high of 6.0950 against the U.S. dollar in the spot market Thursday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to refrain from capping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains this week. Traders are keeping a lookout for China's 3Q GDP data to be released at 0200GMT. Expectations are for a 7.8% gain on quarter. A strong number would set the stage for a resumption of the rally in the Shanghai Composite index, which has recently fallen to its trendline support. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1138 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. The dollar is expected to keep grinding lower, though propped up along the way by \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing the descent. A Friday closing below the immediate technical support at 29.320, which is the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel, may signal more dollar weakness ahead. The dollar took a dump overnight as traders, who increasingly believe that the Federal Reserve will hold back from withdrawing monetary stimulus anytime soon, sold the dollar for higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.320 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.200 (psychological support), before 29.000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.500 (psychological resistance), then at 29.580 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.600 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with downside bias. USD/KRW gapped lower Friday to 1,061.5 from its Thursday close of 1,063.7, as the dollar sank overnight on renewed hopes of easy monetary policy from the U.S. Federal Reserve. The charts have been bearish for USD/KRW for the last couple of weeks, but now, with the dollar already at the base of the Bollinger downtrend channel and near the psychological barrier of 1,060, some consolidation might be at hand. The dollar dropped as low as 1,060.1 before bouncing to 1,062.5 on market chatter of \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  supporting the dollar ahead of the psychological barrier. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,060 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological support), before 1,057 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,068 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance), before 1,073 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--downside bias. USD/SGD is on track toward breaking the base of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2383. A Friday close below this mark would be an additionally bearish signal for the dollar that has been weighed by expectations of continued monetary easing from the U.S. Federal Reserve. Singapore's non-oil exports released Thursday showed the nation exported more than expected on a monthly basis, rising 5.7% versus consensus for a 1.4% gain, though the on-year data shrank. The passing of the U.S. debt-ceiling deal will also add to certainty for the global economy, which is a boon for the Singapore dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2384 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2383 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1.2300 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2400 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2433 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2482 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. The ringgit is now at its strongest level in four months, after the USD/MYR fell below the September low 3.1445. The dollar was last at these levels in June. The broad weakness of the USD stems from renewed confidence that the U.S. Federal Reserve will keep quantitative easing at full pace for longer, given the uncertainty of other \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  policies and the well-known dovishness of incoming Fed chief Janet Yellen. USD/MYR is now inside the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel and may soon fall to the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support at 3.1035. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.1200 (psychological support), then at 3.1035 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.1000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.1470 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), before 3.1690 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--downside bias. USD/THB breaks the technical stalemate at last, falling convincingly into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel late Thursday and cracking the psychological barrier at 31.00. This bearish technical signal could give the go-ahead to traders to sell the dollar, targeting the base of the channel at 30.74. Renewed confidence in a dovish stance from the U.S. Federal Reserve is adding to weakness of the U.S. dollar and increasing investor risk appetite. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.80 (psychological support), then at 30.74 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 31.00 (psychological resistance), then at 31.14 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP may sink toward the bottom of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 42.66 as the dollar slumps across the board in overnight trade. The renewed optimism of a dovish U.S. Federal Reserve seems the be the main driver for dollar weakness. As long as USD/PHP stays below 43.17, the bearish pull of the Bollinger downtrend channel will remain in play. A break of the 43.00 psychological support, a level not tested since June, is expected to trigger more selling of the dollar due to stop-loss orders. China third-quarter GDP to be released later may add to positive investor sentiment and help drive the peso higher against the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.66 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.17 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 43.25 (200-week moving average), before 43.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. An escalation of broad dollar weakness overnight could help the rupiah to gain Friday. The U.S. dollar fell sharply overnight, particularly against the majors, and this could affect traders' views on the USD/IDR as well. USD/IDR may soon head for the 20-day Bollinger mid at 11,120, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem rupiah strength to keep the country's exports attractively priced. The rupiah is the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia this year, down 15.1% to date, mainly due to current account woes and weakening export performance affecting the trade balance as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,200 (psychological support), then at 11,120 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 11,000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,400 (psychological resistance), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,520 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. Dollar weakness appears to be the theme for now, and may continue as such given the rising belief that the U.S. Federal Reserve is going to be more dovish than before, especially with Janet Yellen at the helm. USD/INR dropped into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel late Thursday, a bearish technical indicator for the dollar that could trigger more dollar weakness toward the major psychological support at 60.00. There is also a growing confidence that India is getting its act together, helped by the proactive nature of recently appointed Reserve Bank of India Gov. Raghuram Rajan, who said he would soon reform the banking sector to allow foreign banks entry. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.00 (psychological support), then at 61.50 (psychological support), before 60.00 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.27 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 61.50 (psychological resistance), before 62.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 17, 2013 20:56 ET (00:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131018e9ai00043\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
