\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rupiah weakens past 11,000 for first time since early 2009\b0\par\par\uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2013\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details and background)\par \par \uc2 * Corporate dollar demand keeps weighing on rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Record trade deficit in July is latest worry\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  - traders\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rupiah weakened past the psychologically important level of 11,000 per dollar on Tuesday, for the first time in more than four years, as the market fretted after the government reported a record monthly trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah's indicative prices lost 0.7 percent to 11,050 per dollar, its weakest since April 2009.\par \par \uc2 Monday's announcement that Indonesia's trade deficit in July soared to $2.31 billion, nearly triple the June level, was the latest in a series of blows to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has shed nearly 13 percent against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 The July deficit makes some analysts and traders worry that Indonesia's current account deficit, which widened sharply in the second quarter, could get bigger this quarter, even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects it to narrow.\par \par \uc2 While the rupiah slipped again on Tuesday, Indonesia's benchmark stock index rose 1.5 percent, erasing most of Monday's decline.\par \par \uc2 The latest fall for the rupiah, which shed 0.6 percent on Monday, stemmed from dollar demand from local companies in thin liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Forward markets on Tuesday pointed to further depreciation in the rupiah, with one-month non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) to the dollar weakening to 11,720.\par \par \uc2 The spread between the spot rate and the NDFs widened to 655 basis points. The one-month offshore/onshore forward spread increased to 610 bps.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's spreads were the highest since Aug. 27, when they reached their widest since the global finance crisis in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Scotiabank, in a client note, said the rupiah still faces "significant negative speculative strain", adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "is not yet out of the woods by any stretch of the imagination."\par \par \uc2 According to traders, the rupiah has periodically traded weaker than 11,000 since late August, as banks in Indonesia bought dollars above that for their local corporate clients. However, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  often discouraged dealers from posting on electronic trading platforms price levels weaker than 11,000.\par \par \uc2 SCREEN SHOWINGS\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, screens showed 11,050 rupiah to the dollar, but the rupiah was traded weaker than that level, according to dealers.\par \par \uc2 "BI cannot fight the market," said a Jakarta-based trader, referring to \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  letting the rupiah weaken below 11,000 in the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been providing dollar liquidity and, since June, has raised its benchmark interest rate by 125 basis points to support the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 But deteriorating economic fundamentals could not stop foreign outflows, putting pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, along with the Indian rupee, are seen as especially vulnerable to anticipated reduction in the Federal Reserve's quantitative easing. Both India and Indonesia are struggling with growing current account deficits, slowing economic growth and resistance to implementing much-needed reforms.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have dumped a net 5.9 trillion rupiah ($538.08 million) of Indonesian stocks between Aug. 1 and Sept. 2, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 During August, foreigners also reduced bond holdings by 1.8 trillion rupiah, the government data showed. (Editing by Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | G | IF | M | O | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | DNP | PGE | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130903e993000dv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
