\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 3,189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2013\par 02:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1231-6.1310   6.1200-6.1389 \par USD/TWD   30.060-30.180   30.000-30.300 \par USD/KRW   1,123-1,130     1,120-1,136 \par USD/SGD   1.2800-1.2891   1.2765-1.2900 \par USD/MYR   3.3000-3.3200   3.2830-3.3290 \par USD/THB   32.00-32.49     31.80-32.71 \par USD/PHP   43.70- 44.00    43.50-44.04 \par USD/IDR   10,700-10,800   10,530-11,000 \par USD/INR   64.00-64.50     63.50-65.00 \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY - consolidation, possible upside. The jump in the dollar index overnight could trigger a higher-than-expected USD/CNY central parity rate, but the highlight today will be the \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Flash PMI data due 0145 GMT. A strong reading would buffer the CNY and Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a further routing. Risk appetite is shaky after the Fed released minutes of the July FOMC meeting, which reveals most board members think the Fed is on the right track toward a September tapering of QE. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1231 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1200 (psychological support), before 6.1152 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1310 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1389 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD - upside bias. The USD/TWD could finally see some action now that a catalyst has appeared in the form of the mildly hawkish U.S. Federal Reserve's July FOMC minutes released overnight. USD/TWD is likely to climb out of the Ichimoku Cloud zone and could go on to enter the Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 30.180. Dollar short covering and more U.S. bond selling are pushing the greenback upwards as a September tapering of QE looks highly likely - barring any exceptionally poor data the rest of this month. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.060 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.940 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.180 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.300 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW - upside bias. USD/KRW leaps into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel as the dollar-shorts rush to cover their positions following the hawkish reading of the Fed's July FOMC minutes released overnight. There might be more room on the upside toward the psychological resistance at 1,130, but near that level, \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  could step in to slow the won's decline. The Kospi dropped 0.9% after the opening bell, adding to bearish won sentiment. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,123 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1,120(psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,130 (psychological resistance), then at 1,136 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD - upside bias. USD/SGD is likely to keep rising after the spike overnight which followed the release of the Fed's July FOMC minutes. The dollar will likely be a buy on dips now that the consensus for a September tapering of quantitative easing becomes clearer. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield aiming towards 3.0% is also another factor that is spooking the dollar-shorts and thereby inciting more dollar buying. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2800 (psychological support), then at 1.2765 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2750 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2891 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2900 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR - upside bias. A perfect storm of data and headlines is crushing the ringgit and forcing it to a new 3-year low of 3.3180. The Fed's July FOMC minutes released overnight leans towards keeping to the September taper timeline, which triggered another wave of bond selling and caused the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields, and therefore the dollar, to rise. The disappointing Malaysia 2Q GDP growth and the shrinking current account deficit released late Wednesday also added to bearishness on the ringgit. Traders expect the \uc2 Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to tame the downward spiral of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it might be difficult to prevent the ringgit from weakening eventually as the USD-buying tide gathers momentum. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3000 (major psychological barrier), then at 3.2830 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2570 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3200 (psychological barrier), before 3.3290 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB is likely to keep on rising, boosted by the Fed's July FOMC minutes released overnight which affirms a September tapering of QE. The 'three white soldiers' candlestick pattern has appeared, though contingent on a Thursday closing near its intraday high. Confirmation of this signal would indicate the rally is going to continue, possibly toward the top of the monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 32.71. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.80 (psychological support), before 31.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.49 (monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.71 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP - upside bias. USD/PHP is expected to gap much higher, possibly toward 44.00, after the 3-day break due to the floods and the public holiday. The pair could soon meet resistance at the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 44.04. The greenback has surged over the course of the week, due to expectations of the U.S. Federal Reserve tapering quantitative easing September. Those fears were mostly confirmed by the release of the July FOMC minutes overnight. Dow Jones Technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.70 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.00 (psychological resistance), then at 44.04 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR - upside bias. USD/IDR is possibly on its way to a new psychological barrier at 11,000 as the greenback rockets higher overnight on the release of the Fed's July FOMC minutes, which affirm expectations of a September withdrawal from QE. The rupiah is already at a 4-year high but may easily surpass more historical highs unless \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  puts a firmer foot down to stop the rupiah depreciating. The case for aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be weak though, considering the poor state of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The Indonesia stock market is likely to remain under intense selling pressure even as the local pension funds continue to buy to support the market. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,700 (psychological support), then at 10,530 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 10,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 10,800 (psychological resistance), before 11,000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR - upside bias. The routing of the rupee is likely to continue, fuelled by USD-short covering on the back of the Fed's July FOMC minutes. The rupee fell to yet another record low Wednesday, despite attempts by the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  to quell the panic selling. USD/INR may soon hit 65.00 to the dollar - a target that is not far considering that a 2.0% intraday move in this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not considered unusual anymore. The minutes of the Fed's July FOMC meeting concur that a September tapering of QE is on the cards. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 64.00 (psychological support), then at 63.50 (psychological support), before 63.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 64.55 (record high), then at 65.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 22-08-13 0056GMT ]\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par          Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.1200-6.1228   6.1148-6.1308 \par USD/TWD   30.060-30.180   30.000-30.300 \par USD/KRW   1,120-1,123     1,117-1,125 \par USD/SGD   1.2800-1.2839   1.2771-1.2891 \par USD/MYR   3.3000-3.3200   3.2860-3.3290 \par USD/THB   32.00-32.49     31.80-32.71 \par USD/PHP   44.00- 44.77    43.71-45.00 \par USD/IDR   10,800-10,900   10,700-11,000 \par USD/INR   64.00-65.00     63.50-65.56 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - slight downside bias. USD/CNY could slip out of the Bollinger downtrend channel that now caps at 6.1228, as the dollar firmed up again in overnight trade despite a slightly worse than forecast U.S. weekly jobless claims number. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield stays elevated near 2.90%, adding to dollar support. The PBOC central parity rate could head toward 6.1750 in reaction to the jump in USD/JPY toward 99.00. The Chinese manufacturing industry appears to be turning around faster than expected, based on the upbeat HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI released Thursday, which will have positive knock-on effects for several trade-dependent Asia countries and also resource-exporter Australia. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1200 (psychological support), then at 6.1148 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1090 (record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1228 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1308 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1388 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - upside bias. The USD/TWD will take on a bullish bias if it ends Friday above the Ichimoku Cloud zone which spans 29.850-30.060. The dollar is looking buoyant still, as the chips fall into place for a September withdrawal from U.S. monetary stimulus. Traders will be averse toward shorting the dollar with one glance at the elevated \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield curve. Taiwan industrial production data, to be released at 0800 GMT, could show a slight pickup as the developed nations which Taiwan exporters depend on have been recovering steadily in recent months. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.060 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.940 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.180 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.300 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation, mid-term upside bias. USD/KRW has dipped back to the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel, but may find difficulty heading much higher in the short term as the daily Ichimoku Cloud dangles nearby at 1,123. The fundamental USD strength that has driven USD/KRW above 1,120 this week is unlikely to falter, due to increased certainty that the U.S. Federal Reserve is ending QE soon, which implies that USD/KRW in the medium term is still likely biased higher. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,120 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,117 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 1,123 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 1,125 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,130 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - upside bias. USD/SGD could pullback slightly from the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel due to profit-taking, as risk appetite returns on the back of U.S. stocks recovering overnight and Japan's Nikkei rallying 1.8% this morning. That said, USD/SGD is still biased higher as long as the pair stays above 1.2771 - the base of the uptrend channel. The case for a stronger greenback is unlikely to have changed despite the slightly weaker-than-expected U.S. weekly jobless claims data released Thursday. USD/SGD will likely be a target to buy-on-dips as \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields still indicate a stronger dollar to come. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2800 (psychological support), then at 1.2771 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2750 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2839 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2891 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2900 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - upside bias. The Malaysia ringgit will likely stay under pressure as it becomes more apparent that the U.S. Federal Reserve is going to reduce its pace of bond purchases soon. Despite the much-talked about declining current account surplus that analysts have highlighted is a risk to Malaysia, the government has so far only said that exports will recover in H2 and thereby the current account surplus will also improve. The spike in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields, as bond investors offload their holdings, has been driving the greenback upwards over the past month. Traders have suspected the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Malaysia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of providing a copious volume of dollar liquidity to cap USD/MYR in the spot market and thus buffer the ringgit, but it might be difficult to prevent the ringgit from weakening eventually as the USD fundamentals look more positive than before. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3000 (major psychological barrier), then at 3.2860 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2620 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3200 (psychological barrier), then at 3.3225 (Thursday's 3-year high), before 3.3290 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB appears to be building on the rally seen this week that has taken the pair to a 3-year high of 32.17 in a short span of time. The next target for the pair could be the monthly Bollinger uptrend channel at 32.49, as the U.S. dollar continues to chalk up new multi-year highs against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept interest rates unchanged at its policy meeting Thursday, ignoring the government's stance toward stimulating the stumbling economy. Thai 2Q GDP fell 0.3%, triggering a technical definition of a recession, but the Thai Finance Minister has denied that the country is in recession and instead fingered the BOT for being "slow and unresponsive" to react to the economic slowdown. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.80 (psychological support), before 31.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.49 (monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.71 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - upside bias. USD/PHP will probably stay aloft, despite the chart looking overbought due to the large spike Wednesday which followed the 3-day break. Expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to reduce its bond buying activity continues to keep the dollar elevated. But aside from pure USD strength, peso investors may be jittery after the credit ratings agency S&P warned that the large and concentrated exposure of Philippines banks to a handful of family-run conglomerates is a cause for concern and could lead to a rating review if one of the conglomerates reneges on debt payments. Dow Jones Technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.00 (psychological support), then at 43.71 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 43.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.77 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 45.00 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - upside bias. USD/IDR could pullback Friday as the market anticipates the government to announce new policies to address the country's economic woes. The state of Indonesia's current account deficit, and the lean foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, has led to widespread speculation in recent weeks that the rupiah could fall further, akin to the India rupee. The USD/IDR NDF contracts continue to trade at an exorbitant premium to the spot contract, a sign that dollar liquidity in the onshore market is still thin and investor confidence is low. Once the NDF premium begins to decline, we could see the rupiah stage a more significant recovery. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,800(psychological support), then at 10,700 (psychological support), before 10,530 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 10,900 (psychological resistance), before 11,000 (major psychological barrier).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - pullback lower, but mid-term upside bias. The rupee managed to salvage some of its losses after the government said there are no plans to install capital controls to stop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's freefall. This calmed the market, which had been anticipating a larger exodus of investors taking flight in fear of capital controls to come. The multitude of problems facing India, beginning with its chronic current account deficit, have seen it collapse to an all-time low of 65.56 to the dollar. The government thus far has taken a piecemeal approach toward fixing the trade imbalances, which has been deemed to be of little effect and has instead exacerbated the loss of confidence in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to deal with the situation. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 64.00 (psychological support), then at 63.50 (psychological support), before 63.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 65.00 (psychological resistance), then at 65.56 (record high).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 23-08-13 0056GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130822e98m0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
