\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT: NZD/USD Under Pressure On Broad USD Strength -\uc2 HiFX\b0\par\par\uc2 1,473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 06:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The NZD/USD is under pressure on broad USD strength ahead of the minutes of the last FOMC meeting, due early Thursday in NZ, says Alex Hill, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HiFX\f28 \uc2 \f2 's head of trading. "There is a little bit of preemptive U.S. dollar buying across the board on the suggestion we will see" more talk about tapering, he says, adding downside risk remains for the pair. The NZD/USD is at 0.7935 vs 0.7982 early this morning. Hill puts short-term support at 0.7880, with resistance at 0.8000. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 The NZD/USD is under pressure on broad USD strength ahead of the minutes of the last FOMC meeting, due early Thursday in NZ, says Alex Hill, \uc2 HiFX\uc2 's head of trading. "There is a little bit of preemptive U.S. dollar buying across the board on the suggestion we will see" more talk about tapering, he says, adding downside risk remains for the pair. The NZD/USD is at 0.7935 vs 0.7982 early this morning. Hill puts short-term support at 0.7880, with resistance at 0.8000. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 as USD/IDR hits a new 4-year high and stocks remain under pressure despite local pension-fund buying since late Tuesday. The rupiah falls to 10,760, a further 0.7% depreciation compared to its Tuesday closing, bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a 10.5% trough for the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could drop to the major psychological barrier at 11,000 if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not step in soon. Two local pension funds have been buying stocks to support the equity market, helping to drive the Jakarta Stock Exchange up 1.5% earlier. The JKSE is now up 0.7% despite the pension-fund demand. USD/IDR is now at 10,750. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Most Indonesian companies will be unaffected by the recent fall in the rupiah, Nomura said on Wednesday. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk to corporate balance sheets is not much, in our view, given the aggregate net debt to equity of top-50 corporations (excluding banks) in Indonesia is only 22% as of the first half of 2013," Nomura said in a research note on Wednesday. Indonesian listed companies don't have large foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debt. Companies that don't earn U.S. dollars but have issued U.S. dollar-denominated bonds like PT Astra Internationals subsidiaries PT Federal International Finance and \uc2 PT Astra Sedaya Finance\uc2  have hedged these, it said. "We believe most of the U.S. dollar debts in Indonesia are from [subsidiaries of] foreign-owned companies operating in Indonesia," it said. The biggest problem will be rising costs. "It will take time before [companies] can pass on the cost increase to consumers. The cost pressure issue will be even more delicate this time as wage increase and logistic coast increases have been high," Nomura said. i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0303 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude prices slip in Asia as investors remain cautious ahead of the weekly stockpiles data from the \uc2 U.S. Energy Information Administration\uc2 , due later in the day. In terms of fundamentals, overnight \uc2 American Petroleum Institute\uc2  data looked "bullish," ANZ says in a report; "unrest in Egypt and Libya continued to support the geopolitical risk premium in the market, but market participants could have taken profits ahead of the U.S. FOMC (Federal Open Market Committee) minutes," it adds. October Nymex crude is at $104.86/bbl, down 15 cents and October Brent crude is at $109.76/bbl, 39 cents lower from its previous close. Meanwhile, a distillation unit at Venezuela's largest oil refiner-Amuay-was halted after a strike caused a fore to break out at the 80,000-barrels-a-day unit. Amuay has total processing capacity of 645,000 barrels a day. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 The USD/JPY is lower on a decline in the Tokyo stock market after its initial gain and partly due to news that \uc2 Japan's Nuclear Regulation Authority\uc2  says the latest Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant leak is a "Level 3" or a "serious radiation incident." A senior dealer at a major Japanese bank says the news appeared to knock stocks down first before prompting JPY-buying on views that investor risk sentiment will be further undermined. "But I doubt this news will have a lasting impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the leakage itself is nothing new," the dealer says. The pair is at 97.17 after it rose earlier to 97.57. The Nikkei falls 0.8%. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 The yuan is trading slightly higher against the U.S. dollar, tracking the euro's strength overnight and a stronger yuan reference exchange rate. The USD/CNY is at 6.1216, down from 6.1246 late Tuesday. Earlier, the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar-yuan central parity rate at 6.1675, down from 6.1697 yesterday. However, fresh signs of capital outflows from China and the recent selloff in Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cap the yuan's upside, traders say. "People are still waiting for more action but we could see some selling pressure on the yuan as well," says a trader at a large domestic bank in Shanghai. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY nondeliverable forward contracts are at 6.2495/6.2570, up from 6.2450/6.2485 late Tuesday.(hong.shen@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 awaited later in the global day is likely to keep dollar subdued. The USD/KRW is likely to be trapped by the daily Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1) for now as traders may take a wait-and-see approach instead of chasing the dollar around. Expectations are high for the Fed to begin tapering monetary stimulus next month, and tonight's release of the FOMC minutes could confirm this belief and thus send the dollar higher. USD/KRW is now 1,119.2. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0.9% Wednesday. The rupiah continues to be under selling pressure, which may prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it did Tuesday. USD/IDR notches a new 4-year high of 10,740 and may be on its way to the major psychological barrier at 11,000. The Jakarta Stock Exchange, which at its Tuesday trough was down more than 10% for the week, is bouncing slightly, up 0.9% so far, possibly on profit-taking from investors with short positions. USD/IDR is now at 10,730. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 The USD/MYR is slightly higher at 3.2900 vs late Tuesday's 3.2870 in Asia, with the persistently strong upside bias showing no signs of abating. "...a clear break of the psychologically 3.3000 level will likely lead to an acceleration higher towards the next resistance at 3.3300," says UOB, noting that the prevailing uncertainties surrounding emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  signal upside risk. The house expects the trend-line support at 3.2300 to hold for the "next couple of weeks." (jason.ng@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 due 1000GMT which might show the country falling into a current account deficit for the first time since 1997. Technical analysis suggests the pair has an upside bias within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, potentially to the major psychological trading barrier at 3.3000. The Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, and will likely do so as well today, to slow the pace of ringgit depreciation. Bank Negara appears to be defending the 3.3000 psychological barrier as the ringgit is already at a 3-year low. The ringgit has been falling on speculation that shrinking exports will throw the country into the list of countries with a current account deficit - along with the likes of Indonesia and India. USD/MYR is now 3.2900. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0218 GMT [Dow Jones] A better-than-expected price performance in gold surprised her and the market, Helen Lau, a senior analyst at UOB Kay Hian, says in a report. She notes that positive catalysts for gold prices are better-than-expected physical demand in China, inflows into gold exchange-traded funds, strength of the USD and the impact of winding down of liquidity by the U.S. Federal Reserve. She also notes that some of UOB's clients are "tempted" to add exposure to gold via ETFs. "They are searching for positive catalysts or contrarian view on gold," Lau says. Spot gold is at $1,372/oz, up $1 from its previous close. (arpan.mukherjee@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 21, 2013 00:50 ET (04:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130821e98l0011c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
