\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.1234-6.1312   6.1200-6.1391 \par USD/TWD          -               - \par USD/KRW    1,116-1,120     1,112-1,123 \par USD/SGD    1.2734-1.2785   1.2700-1.2800 \par USD/MYR    3.2750-3.3000   3.2510-3.3220 \par USD/THB    31.50-31.71     31.34-32.00 \par USD/PHP          -               - \par USD/IDR    10,500-10,700   10,300-10,800 \par USD/INR    63.00-63.50     62.50-64.00 \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY - downside bias. PBOC will likely set the benchmark USD/CNY exchange rate lower in line with the dollar's overnight slide. This may exert downwards pressure on spot USD/CNY and push it back into the Bollinger downtrend channel. Further dollar direction may however depend on the tone of the minutes from the U.S. Federal Reserve's last FOMC meeting. The Fed will release the minutes of its last FOMC meeting later today. Data watchers will also be looking ahead to Thursday's China HSBC Flash Manufacturing PMI for an indication as to how the economy is growing. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1234 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1200 (psychological support), before 6.1156 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1312 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1391 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD - closed due to storm.\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW - consolidation. USD/KRW may hover between a 1,112-1,120 range for now, as the dollar subsides overnight ahead of the release of the July FOMC minutes. The USD/KRW is likely to be trapped by the daily Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1) for now as traders may take a wait-and-see approach instead of chasing the dollar lower. Expectations are high for the Fed to begin tapering monetary stimulus next month, and the release of the FOMC minutes could confirm this belief. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,116 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1,112 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,110 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,120 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,123 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1,124 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD - upside bias. USD/SGD retains a bullish bias, despite the greenback selloff overnight. The pair remains within the Bollinger uptrend channel, which now supports at 1.2734, and also above the daily Ichimoku Cloud - together creating a fairly bullish signal that could propel the pair toward its year-high of 1.2859. Traders are awaiting today's release of the U.S. Federal Reserve July FOMC minutes for further hints as to when the tapering of QE might begin. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2734 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2689 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2785 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2859 (2013 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR - upside bias. Traders are eagerly awaiting today's release of Malaysia's GDP figures as well as Balance of Payments data, which might show the country falling into a current account deficit for the first time since 1997. Technical analysis suggests the daily Bollinger uptrend channel continues to pull USD/MYR upwards, potentially to the major psychological trading barrier at 3.3000. The \uc2 Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday to slow the pace of ringgit depreciation, seemingly to protect the 3.3000 barrier as the ringgit is already at a 3-year low. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2750 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2510 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 3.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3000 (major psychological barrier and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3220 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB - upside bias. A bullish stance appears, after USD/THB popped higher Tuesday as the emerging Asia selloff appears to be spreading to Thailand as well. The dollar spiked to as high as 31.72, but eased overnight as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields subsided. the dollar is likely to be bought on dips as investors position for a potential hawkish tone in the Fed's July FOMC minutes - a signal that an end to QE is coming soon. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.50 (psychological support), then at 31.34 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before at 31.20 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.71 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP - closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR - consolidation with upside bias. The rupiah could recoup some losses as dollar strength eases ahead of the July FOMC minutes due later in the global day. The Indonesia stock market selloff has been grabbing headlines this week, falling more than 10% in two days. The rupiah has therefore come under intense selling pressure as well, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars in the spot market. This could help quell the investor panic for now, but the country's slowing growth, high inflation and widening current account deficit will continue to worry. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last Thursday said the risk of slowing growth "remains significant". Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,530 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 10,500 (psychological support), before 10,300 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 10,700 (psychological resistance), before 10,800 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR - consolidation with upside bias. The rupee recovered late Tuesday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 , in a reversal of a decision made in July, announced it would purchase more government bonds to increase rupee liquidity. The change of heart comes as the rupee hit a third consecutive record low. USD/INR could therefore subside as the bearish bets on the rupee could be trimmed a little on the government backtracking on recently tightened liquidity measures. But the highlight of the week - U.S. July FOMC minutes to be released later today - could easily turn the dollar higher again if it hints at a September tapering of U.S. monetary stimulus. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.00 (psychological support), then at 62.50 (psychological support), before 62.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 63.50 (psychological resistance), then at 64.00 (psychological support), before 64.11.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 21-08-13 0047GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130821e98l0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
