\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  Asia Takes Strain As Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Selloff Continues\b0\par\par\uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 15:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Selling pressure on Indian rupee, Indonesian rupiah continues\par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  suspected of taking action to support rupiah, dealers say\par \par \uc2 --Turkey rate decision due at 1100 GMT\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 The selloff in Asian emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  intensified Tuesday with the Indian rupee plunging to a new life-time low, while the Indonesian rupiah fell to its weakest level since April 2009, amid concerns over how these countries will cope when the Federal Reserve starts withdrawing stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 The rupee remained locked in a downward spiral Tuesday, falling to a fresh record low against the greenback of INR64.11. The Indonesian rupiah also felt the pain, slumping to a four-year low of IDR10,700 against the dollar, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually doesn't comment on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Thai baht also weakened to a one-year low, as expectations grew that minutes from the Fed's August meeting due Wednesday could signal that it will start pulling back from the stimulus measures that have supported markets for nearly five years, as early as September.\par \par \uc2 "The action in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently is in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the selloff continues in earnest," said \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of the Fed pulling back on its bond purchases has made investors fret that the tide of money that flowed into emerging markets in recent years will diminish. Countries such as India, which have large current-account deficits, reflecting a reliance on inflows of capital, have felt the brunt of investors fleeing emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has lost more than 5% in value against the dollar so far this month, despite authorites there taking a number measures to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But unless authories take more steps to bolster foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves that could be used to defend the rupee, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to stabilize, analysts say. "This will likely require the issuance of either a Non-resident Indian bond or a sovereign bond," said Indranil Sen Gupta, an analyst at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Europe's emerging markets were calmer. The Hungarian forint and Polish zloty, regained some ground against the euro following Monday's selloff.\par \par \uc2 The Turish lira bounced off record lows against the euro and one-month lows against the dollar, ahead of an interest rate decision at 1100 GMT. According to eight economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep the benchmark one-week repo rate at 4.5%, the overnight borrowing rate at 3.5% and the overnight lending rate of 7.25%.\par \par \uc2 "I expect Turkey to stay on hold," said Christian Lawrence of \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 . But he does not rule out the chance that the lending rate may be raised by 0.5 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 In the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors piled into the perceived safe havens of the yen and Swiss franc, with the former rising to one-week high against the dollar and the latter a one-week high against the euro\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the New Zealand dollar came under pressure against the buck after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  said it will introduce new restrictions on home loans in October.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar also weakened against the U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said there is the possibility of a further cut in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 In minutes of its Aug. 6 policy meeting--when the benchmark cash rate was cut to a record low 2.50%--the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  said it will continue to watch economic data to assess the correct level of interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "Regarding the communication of this decision, members agreed that the bank should neither close off the possibility of reducing rates further, nor signal an imminent intention to reduce rates further," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 The Norwegian krone fell to a six-week low against the euro after data showed Norway's economic growth was lower than expected in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 At 1030 GMT, the euro was trading at $1.3400 against the dollar, compared with $1.3340, late Monday in New York, according to trading system EBS. The dollar was at Y97.230 against the yen, compared with Y97.57, while the euro was at Y130.27, compared with Y130.11. The pound was trading at $1.5670 against the dollar, compared with $1.5654 late Monday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 73.43 from 73.568.\par \par \uc2 (James Glynn in Sydney contributed to this story.)\par \par \uc2 Write to Clare Connaghan at clare.connaghan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 20-08-13 1320GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130820e98k000fe\par }\page {\par\fs2