\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2013\par 02:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.1186-6.1200   6.1143-6.1322 \par USD/TWD    29.930-30.000   29.850-30.040 \par USD/KRW          -               - \par USD/SGD    1.2675-1.2700   1.2619-1.2751 \par USD/MYR    3.2600-3.2800   3.2500-3.2900 \par USD/THB     31.20-31.27     31.07-31.47 \par USD/PHP     43.71-44.00     43.50-44.17 \par USD/IDR    10,215-10,300   10,200-10,390 \par USD/INR          -               - \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation with bearish bias. USD/CNY can be expected to consolidate with a bearish bias as the dollar remains inside the Bollinger downtrend channel that now caps at 6.1259. The PBOC dollar/yuan parity rate may be shifted a tad lower in line with a slight pullback in dollar strength. A risk aversion stemming from Wall Street's overnight losses could weigh on Chinese stock markets. China Foreign Direct Investment numbers due at 0200 GMT will be in the spotlight later. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at, then at 6.1186 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1143 (all-time low), before 6.1100 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1200 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1259 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1322 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to remain trapped by the daily Ichimoku Cloud zone that spans 29.850-30.040. The 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line meets the Cloud top at 30.040, adding to the strength of the technical trading barrier, and will likely keep a lid on the dollar. The greenback steadied overnight after Federal Reserve member James Bullard delivered a mildly dovish tone in his speech Wednesday, saying that the Fed needs to evaluate more data before deciding when to taper. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.930 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.850 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 29.800 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.040 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.180 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- mild upside bias. USD/SGD has climbed above the daily Ichimoku Cloud -- a mild bullish signal -- but failed to enter the nearby Bollinger uptrend channel, thus dulling the potential for a further rally. The appearance of the two bullish technical signals together would increase the likelihood of a larger rally toward 1.2800. A Thursday close above 1.2706 would trigger the daily Bollinger uptrend channel into play. U.S. dollar demand is likely to persist, on the back of the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield hovering above 2.70% despite slightly dovish talk from Federal Reserve board member James Bullard. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2675 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 1.2662 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2619 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2700 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2706 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2751 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- upside bias. The U.S. dollar remains biased higher against the Malaysia ringgit, as long as the USD/MYR pair stays above 3.2600 Thursday -- which would cement its place inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. The next target for the pair is the top of the channel at 3.2900, though it is expected to be a slow grind higher due to market chatter that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been providing dollar liquidity to slow the ringgit's decline. Investors may be awaiting the release of Malaysia's Balance of Payments data due Aug 21, which could reveal the 2Q current account deficit that analysts have been predicting -- which is the main reason why the ringgit has fallen so much since mid-July. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2600 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2500 (psychological support), before 3.2300 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2800 (psychological resistance), then at 3.2900 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation. USD/THB may stabilize after it tried but failed to enter the Bollinger uptrend channel Wednesday. The U.S. dollar is a tad weaker overnight but not likely to fall much in Asia due to a mild risk aversion sparked by the overnight U.S. equity selloff. The USD/THB could range within 31.07-31.27 for now. U.S. weekly jobless claims data due later in the global day may trigger the next move in the dollar, if the number surprises significantly in either direction. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.20 (psychological support), then at 31.07 (20-day Bollinger mid and Ichimoku Cloud support), before 31.00 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 31.27 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.47 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- upside bias. USD/PHP will retain its bullish stance as long as it manages to keep its head above the 43.71 base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The dollar is a tad weaker overnight but the risk aversion forming in Asia, where Japan's Nikkei has dropped 1.2%, may make it difficult for emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate. If the Bollinger uptrend channel remains in play, the next big target for USD/PHP is the 44.00 psychological barrier. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.71 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 43.50 (psychological support), before 43.40 (200-week moving average). Immediate resistance is at 44.00 (psychological resistance), then at 44.13 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.17 (year-high).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- upside bias. The USD/IDR notched a new 4-year high of 10,290 to the dollar, but may not trade much higher in the near term with likely \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  slowing the pace of the rupiah's decline. The pair was conspicuously stable Wednesday, which hints at the presence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor has also said in recent months that the rupiah's weakness is in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Malaysia ringgit, which suggests that more 'controlled' weakness may be in store. Malaysia's ringgit fell to a new 3-year low Wednesday and looks on track to fall further. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,215 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 10,200 (psychological support), before 10,045 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 10,300 (psychological resistance), then at 10,390 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 10,550 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- closed.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 14, 2013 20:32 ET (00:32 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130815e98f0006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
