\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT: Indonesia's rupiah marks new 4-year low of 10,290 per dollar....\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2013\par 07:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The USD/IDR rises again on broad dollar strength, notching a new 4-year high of 10,290 to the dollar. The pair looks conspicuously stable Wednesday, which may hint at the presence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- to prevent excessive rupiah weakness. Still, the Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor has said in recent months that the rupiah's weakness is in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Malaysia ringgit, which suggests that more weakness may be in store. Malaysia's ringgit fell to a new 3-year low earlier. The USD/IDR is recently at 10,290.\par \par \uc2 (ewen.chew@dowjones.com @djfxtrader)\par \par \uc2 (Ewen Chew is an Asia-Pacific \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporter at Dow Jones Newswires. Previously, he was an Asia NDF trader for five years, focusing on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia and the Philippines.) [ 14-08-13 0539GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130814e98e0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
