with their own financial, \par                                                                           legal, and accounting advisors about \par                                                                           the risks associated with an investment \par                                                                           in these Notes, the appropriate tools \par                                                                           to analyze that investment, and the \par                                                                           suitability of the investment in \par                                                                           each investor's particular circumstances. \par                                                                           Holders of the Notes should also \par                                                                           consult with their professional tax \par                                                                           advisors regarding tax laws applicable \par                                                                           to them and, in particular, with \par                                                                           respect to tax laws relating to debt \par                                                                           securities in bearer form. \par  \par                                                                           The Bank may hedge its obligations \par                                                                           under the Notes by entering into \par                                                                           a swap transaction with the Dealer \par                                                                           or one of its affiliates as swap \par                                                                           counterparty. Assuming no change \par                                                                           in market conditions or any other \par                                                                           relevant factors, the price, if any, \par                                                                           at which the Dealer or another purchaser \par                                                                           might be willing to purchase Notes \par                                                                           in a secondary market transaction \par                                                                           is expected to be lower, and could \par                                                                           be substantially lower, than the \par                                                                           original issue price of the Notes. \par                                                                           This is due to a number of factors, \par                                                                           including that (i) the potential \par                                                                           profit to the secondary market purchaser \par                                                                           of the Notes may be incorporated \par                                                                           into any offered price and (ii) the \par                                                                           cost of funding used to value the \par                                                                           Notes in the secondary market is \par                                                                           expected to be higher than our actual \par                                                                           cost of funding incurred in connection \par                                                                           with the issuance of the Notes. In \par                                                                           addition, the original issue price \par                                                                           of the Notes included, and secondary \par                                                                           market prices are likely to exclude, \par                                                                           the projected profit that our swap \par                                                                           counterparty or its affiliates may \par                                                                           realize in connection with this swap. \par                                                                           Further, as a result of dealer discounts, \par                                                                           mark-ups or other transaction costs, \par                                                                           any of which may be significant, \par                                                                           the original issue price may differ \par                                                                           from values determined by pricing \par                                                                           models used by our swap counterparty \par                                                                           or other potential purchasers of \par                                                                           the Notes in secondary market transactions. \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information regarding the Notes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. The EU has adopted a Directive regarding the taxation of savings income (the "Savings Directive"). The Savings Directive requires Member States (as defined below) to provide to the tax authorities of other Member States details of payments of interest and other similar income paid by a person to an individual in another Member State, except that Austria and Luxembourg will instead impose a withholding system for a transitional period unless during such period they elect otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank undertakes that it will ensure that it maintains a paying agent in a country which is a member of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  (a "Member State") that will not be obliged to withhold or deduct tax pursuant to the Savings Directive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         United States Federal Income Tax Matters \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-08-13 1645GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United States Internal Revenue Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  Circular 230 Notice: To ensure compliance with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Internal Revenue Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  Circular 230, prospective investors are hereby notified that: (a) any discussion of U.S. federal tax issues contained or referred to in this Pricing Supplement, the Prospectus or any other document referred to herein is not intended or written to be used, and cannot be used, by prospective investors for the purpose of avoiding penalties that may be imposed on them under the United States Internal Revenue Code; (b) such discussions are written for use in connection with the promotion or marketing of the transactions or matters addressed herein; and (c) prospective investors should seek advice based on their particular circumstances from an independent tax advisor.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following supplements the discussion under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus regarding the U.S. federal income tax treatment of the Notes, and is subject to the limitations and exceptions set forth therein. Any tax disclosure in the Prospectus or this pricing supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Due to a change in law since the date of the Prospectus, the second paragraph of "-Payments of Interest" under the United States Holders section should be read as follows: "Interest paid by the Bank on the Notes constitutes income from sources outside the United States and will, depending on the circumstances, be "passive" or "general" income for purposes of computing the foreign tax credit."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information with Respect to Foreign Financial Assets. Owners of "specified foreign financial assets" with an aggregate value in excess of $50,000 (and in some circumstances, a higher threshold) may be required to file an information report with respect to such assets with their tax returns. "Specified foreign financial assets" may include financial accounts maintained by foreign financial institutions (which may include the Notes), as well as the following, but only if they are not held in accounts maintained by financial institutions: (i) stocks and securities issued by non-United States persons, (ii) financial instruments and contracts held for investment that have non-United States issuers or counterparties, and (iii) interests in foreign entities. Holders are urged to consult their tax advisors regarding the application of this reporting obligation to their ownership of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Medicare Tax. For taxable years beginning after December 31, 2012, a U.S. holder that is an individual or estate, or a trust that does not fall into a special class of trusts that is exempt from such tax, will be subject to a 3.8% tax (the "Medicare tax") on the lesser of (1) the U.S. holder's "net investment income" for the relevant taxable year and (2) the excess of the U.S. holder's modified adjusted gross income for the taxable year over a certain threshold (which in the case of individuals will be between $125,000 and $250,000, depending on the individual's circumstances). A holder's net investment income will generally include its gross interest income and its net gains from the disposition of Notes, unless such interest payments or net gains are derived in the ordinary course of the conduct of a trade or business (other than a trade or business that consists of certain passive or trading activities). If you are a U.S. holder that is an individual, estate or trust, you are urged to consult your tax advisors regarding the applicability of the Medicare tax to your income and gains in respect of your investment in the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates may be volatile and may affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in exchange rates between the Indonesian Rupiah and the specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Name: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Edward Bartholomew\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Title:     Chief Financial Officer and General Manager, \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Department\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Annex to Pricing Supplement, IDB Series No. 447\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Applicable Definitions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "IDR Business Day" means a day on which commercial banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets settle payments in Tokyo, New York, Singapore and Jakarta.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "IDR Rate" means, in respect of an IDR Valuation Date, the IDR/JPY exchange rate, expressed as the amount of JPY per one IDR, which is calculated by the Calculation Agent in accordance with the following formula and rounded to the nearest five decimal places with 0.000005 being rounded up:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY Reference Rate divided by USD/IDR Reference Rate\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "IDR Valuation Date" means the day that is five (5) Relevant Business Days prior to the relevant Fixed Rate Interest Payment Date or the Maturity Date, as applicable (a "Scheduled IDR Valuation Date"), or, if such day is an Unscheduled Holiday, the immediately following Relevant Business Day, in which case the related Fixed Rate Interest Payment Date or the Maturity Date, as applicable, shall be postponed to fall five (5) Relevant Business Days after such deferred IDR Valuation Date; provided that, if the IDR Valuation Date has not occurred on or before the tenth (10(th) ) consecutive day after the Scheduled IDR Valuation Date, then the next day after such tenth (10(th) ) day that would have been a Relevant Business Day but for the Unscheduled Holiday shall be deemed to be the IDR Valuation Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Reference Dealers" means five banks active in the USD/IDR or USD/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, as applicable, as selected by the Calculation Agent in its sole discretion, acting in good faith and in a commercially reasonable manner.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Unscheduled Holiday" means a day that is not a Relevant Business Day and the market was not aware of such fact (by means of a public announcement or by reference to other publicly available information) until a time later than 9:00 a.m. local time in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 principal financial\f28 \uc2 \f2  centre(s) of IDR five (5) Relevant Business Days prior to the Scheduled IDR Valuation Date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "USD" means United States dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "USD/IDR Reference Rate" means the spot rate of USD/IDR at 11:00 a.m. Singapore time expressed as the number of IDR per one USD and published on the Reuters Screen "ABSIRFIX01" page (or its successor page for the purpose of displaying such rate) on the applicable IDR Valuation Date, as determined by the Calculation Agent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the event that no such quotation appears on the Reuters Screen "ABSIRFIX01" page (or its successor page for the purpose of displaying such rate), the USD/IDR Reference Rate shall be determined by the Calculation Agent by requesting quotations for mid rate of USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate at or about 11:00 a.m. Singapore time on the first (1st) IDR Business Day following the relevant IDR Valuation Date from the Reference Dealers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If five or four quotations are provided as requested, the USD/IDR Reference Rate will be the arithmetic mean (rounded to the nearest whole IDR, 0.5 being rounded upwards) of the remaining three or two such quotations, as the case may be, for such rate provided by the Reference Dealers, after disregarding the highest such quotation and the lowest such quotation (provided that, if two or more such quotations are the highest such quotations, then only one of such quotations shall be disregarded, and if two or more such quotations are the lowest quotations, then only one of such lowest quotations will be disregarded).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If only three or two such quotations are provided as requested, the USD/IDR Reference Rate shall be determined as described above except that the highest and lowest quotations will not be disregarded.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If none or only one of the Reference Dealers provides such quotation, the USD/IDR Reference Rate will be determined by the Calculation Agent in its sole discretion, acting in good faith and in a commercially reasonable manner.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "USD/JPY Reference Rate" means the mid rate of USD/JPY, expressed as the number of JPY per one USD, published on the Reuters Screen "JPNU" page (or its successor page for the purpose of displaying such rate) as of 12:00 p.m., Tokyo time on the applicable IDR Valuation Date, as determined by the Calculation Agent. [ 12-08-13 1645GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the event that no such quotation appears on the Reuters Screen "JPNU" page (or its successor page for the purpose of displaying such rate), the USD/JPY Reference Rate shall be determined by the Calculation Agent by requesting quotations for mid rate of USD/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate at or about 12:00 p.m. Tokyo time on the first (1st) IDR Business Day following the relevant IDR Valuation Date from Reference Dealers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If five or four quotations are provided as requested, the USD/JPY Reference Rate will be the arithmetic mean of the remaining three or two such quotations, as the case may be, for such rate provided by the Reference Dealers, after disregarding the highest such quotation and the lowest such quotation (provided that, if two or more such quotations are the highest such quotations, then only one of such quotations shall be disregarded, and if two or more such quotations are the lowest quotations, then only one of such lowest quotations will be disregarded).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If only three or two such quotations are provided as requested, the USD/JPY Reference Rate shall be determined as described above except that the highest and lowest quotations will not be disregarded.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If none or only one of the Reference Dealers provides such quotation, the USD/JPY Reference Rate will be determined by the Calculation Agent in its sole discretion, acting in good faith and in a commercially reasonable manner.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IODUUSNROSAWAAR [ 12-08-13 1645GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020130812e98c000s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\