\par\par \b \uc2 STOCKS NEWS INDONESIA-Telkom rises on Q2 earnings\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2013\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia\uc2  rose as much as 3.1 percent after the telecom provider announced its second-quarter results.\par \par \uc2 Net profit grew 12.7 percent to 10.1 trillion rupiah ($1.01 billion) year-on-year, Telkom said in statement on Friday. The company's shares had the second-highest turnover on the stock exchange.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian blue-chip stocks rose 0.02 percent, while the broader Jakarta Composite Index was up 0.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 1510 (0810 GMT)\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 10,060 rupiah)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andjarsari Paramaditha in Jakarta; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu)\par \par \uc2 ***************************************************************  13:30 STOCKS NEWS INDONESIA-Property, utility firms' earnings could beat forecasts-Citi Citi Research expects a weak second-quarter for commodity-related and auto sector companies, while property, media and utility firms could beat consensus estimates, it said in a note on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Property companies are to benefit from strong pre-marketing sales last year, the note said. Media companies could book higher advertising rates, while utilities would benefit primarily from \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.\par \par \uc2 Plantation's downside could be due to higher labour costs and lower crude palm oil prices, while plunging spot coal prices on weak demand from China and India could hurt mining earnings. Auto firms would also be under pressure due to price discounts linked to competition and a weaker rupiah, the note said.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the volatility in the market will continue due to fears of QE tapering and slower China growth of around 7 percent," the note stated.\par \par \uc2 "On the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 -specific front, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , letting the rupiah weaken in line with the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We expect inflation to peak in July, and see a slight improvement in the current account due to the fuel price adjustment."\par \par \uc2 Citi's top picks includes property developers \uc2 Alam Sutera Realty\uc2  and \uc2 Bumi Serpong Damai\uc2 , television operator \uc2 Media Nusantara Citra\uc2 , cement maker Indocement Tunggal Perkasa and toll road operator \uc2 Jasa Marga\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alam Sutera shares were up 1.77 percent at 780 rupiah.\par \par \uc2 The broader index was up 0.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 1328 (0628 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andjarsari Paramaditha in Jakarta; Editing by Prateek Chatterjee)\par \par \uc2 ***************************************************************  11:20 STOCKS NEWS INDONESIA-Bahana cuts Bank Danamon to 'reduce'\par \par \uc2 Bahana Securities\uc2  downgraded lender PT Bank Danamon Tbk  to "reduce" from "hold", citing earnings pressure due to lower margins and additional provisioning and delay in an acquisition deal.     "Going forward, we believe that margin pressure will persist on the back of higher blended cost of funds and intensifying competition in mass market loans," analyst Teguh Hartanto said in a note on Friday.     The research house also said the delay in an acquisition deal due to pending approval from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resulted in uncertainties in the outlook on Danamon.     Last month, \uc2 DBS Group Holdings Ltd\uc2  said it could review its planned acquisition of a stake in Danamon if the Singapore lender was allowed to buy only a 40 percent share.      "Unfortunately, this has become a controversy issue as BI recently revamped regulation on acquisition, limiting ownership of financial institutions in a bank up to 40 percent, implying share acquisitions of more than 40 percent must be transacted through several stages, subject to BI's reviews on healthiness and GCG rating," Hartanto said.     Bahana also slashed its target price on Danamon's shares to 4,500 rupiah from 5,800 and said the company's weak second-quarter earnings prompted the research house to lower its mass-market loan growth estimates for 2013 and 2014 by 13 and 17 percent, respectively.     The lender's shares dropped 1.75 percent to 5,600 rupiah. The broader index was up 0.37 percent.     1111 (0411 GMT)     (Reporting by Andjarsari Paramaditha, Editing by Anupama Dwivedi)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDONESIA-STOCKSNEWS/TELKOM | DNP | ABN | E | RBN | IF | RNP | SI   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130719e97j000bs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
