\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.1404-6.1426   6.1353-6.1500 \par USD/TWD    29.900-30.000   29.820-30.050 \par USD/KRW     1,120-1,126     1,117-1,130 \par USD/SGD    1.2622-1.2687   1.2600-1.2700 \par USD/MYR    3.1850-3.2000   3.1700-3.2150 \par USD/THB     31.00-31.15     30.80-31.20 \par USD/PHP     43.19-43.47     43.00-43.50 \par USD/IDR    10,000-10,130    9,950-10,200 \par USD/INR     59.50-59.83     59.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- possible upside bias. Traders are expecting another high USD/CNY central parity rate, based on the rally in USD/JPY overnight. The daily yuan fixing may come in above 6.1750 and thus pull spot USD/CNY into the Bollinger uptrend channel at 6.1426; the pair closed Thursday at 6.1413. Entry in the Bollinger uptrend channel could motivate some traders to bet on a weaker yuan in the near term. The Shanghai Composite index, which declined in the last two sessions, may find support from U.S. stocks which hit record highs overnight and thus could help bolster yuan weakness. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1404 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 6.1353 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1280 (Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1426 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.1500 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- rebound in play. USD/TWD continues to look bullish in the near term, targeting the 20-day Bollinger mid at 30.050 and then the Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.200. The rebound that began Wednesday when the dollar bounced off the Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 29.820 is still in play. If the USD/TWD pair manages to close Friday above the 20-day Bollinger mid at 30.050, more upside may be in store next week. One of the drivers for a stronger USD/TWD is the rise of the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield back above 2.50%; the benchmark yield is currently around 2.53%. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.900 (Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.820 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 29.750 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.050 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.200 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- likely downside bias. USD/KRW remains within the Bollinger downtrend channel for now, after opening just under the ceiling of the channel which caps near 1,126. If the pair ends Friday above 1,126, the downside momentum would be negated and the dollar could rally higher. But if the Bollinger downtrend channel remains in play, the USD/KRW pair could slide back down to the Ichimoku Cloud support at 1,114-1,117 again. Traders may be watching the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, which is back above 2.50% again, for hints as to the dollar's direction. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,120 (psychological support), then at 1,117 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1,114 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1,126 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,130 (psychological resistance), before 1,139 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- consolidation. USD/SGD is now within a technical consolidation zone and likely to range within 1.2622-1.2687 for now. Conflicting factors point to consolidation for USD/SGD. The greenback may remain firm due to the rebound in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield back above 2.50%, while fresh record highs in U.S. stock markets may help Singapore's STI to rally, and this could bolster the Sing dollar against weakness. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2622 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2600 (psychological support), before 1.2557 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2687 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2700 (psychological resistance), before 1.2753 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- consolidation. USD/MYR is likely to remain in consolidation mode between 3.1850-3.2000. The USD/MYR pair needs to break above 3.2000 or below 3.1850 to change direction in a bigger way. The dollar index rose slightly overnight due to the bump up in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, but risk appetite is likely to be healthy in Asia because of record highs set on Wall Street overnight, and this could support emerging market assets such as the Malaysia ringgit. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.1850 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.1700 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.1550 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2000 (major psychological resistance and Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2150 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation. USD/THB rises back above 31.00 and may hover around this level for now. Thursday's foray into sub-31.00 territory was short-lived, which suggests that dollar-buying on dips is prevalent and may have spooked some dollar bears into covering their positions. The pair is likely to be capped by the Bollinger uptrend channel which begins at 31.15; but a Friday close above this mark could mean more upside next week. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.00 (psychological barrier), then at 30.80 (psychological support), before 30.60 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 31.15 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.20 (psychological resistance), before 31.35 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation. USD/PHP may find difficulty rallying due to the 200-week moving average at 43.47 acting as a resistance level and the daily Bollinger uptrend channel also capping the pair at 43.53. Thus the dollar may consolidate with a slightly bearish bias. The greenback is slightly firmer across the board due to the rise of the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield back above the 2.50% mark. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.19 (intraweek low), then at 43.00 (major psychological support), before 42.58 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 43.47 (200-week moving average), then at 43.50 (psychological resistance), before 43.53 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- upside bias. The dollar may continue to rise against the Indonesia rupiah, now that Bernanke's testimony to Congress is out of the way. USD/IDR could aim for the next barrier at 10,100 before attempting to hit the top of the monthly Bollinger uptrend channel at 10,130. U.S. Treasuries are getting sold off again, driving the benchmark 10-year yield higher above 2.50% once more and thus lifting the dollar broadly. A lack of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also paving the way for an even weaker rupiah in the near term. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,000 (major psychological support), then at 9,955 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,900 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 10,130 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 10,200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation, possible upside bias. USD/INR is currently capped by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 59.83, but the bullish candlestick Thursday suggests that the USD/INR rally may have more upside momentum. A Friday close above 59.83 could lead to a resumption of rupee weakness over the next week. The greenback is broadly stronger even after Federal Reserve chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  sought to allay fears of an immediate pullout from quantitative easing. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose above 2.50% overnight and is likely to support the dollar. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.50 (psychological support), then at 59.00 (psychological support), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 59.83 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 60.00 (major psychological resistance), before 60.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 19-07-13 0047GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130719e97j0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
