\par\par \b \uc2 Asian c.banks take differing approaches to stemming outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 By Randy Fabi and Rieka Rahadiana   \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2013\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, July 10 (Reuters) - Asian central banks are expected to adopt divergent strategies to protect their economies against weaker growth and scary foreign capital outflows as they hold policy reviews amid a sea-change in international markets.\par \par \uc2 For much of Asia, the prospect of the U.S. Federal Reserve winding down its easy money policies has removed the headache of asset-inflating inflows, though the speed at which funds have pulled out has created a whole new set of worries for some.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in Indonesia and India, which rely on foreign capital to fund current account deficits and are therefore more vulnerable to portfolio outflows, have been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to defend their weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to hike its benchmark policy rate for a second consecutive month at a policy review on Thursday, and could announce surprise measures to counter surging inflation, a declining rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and falling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "The limelight is certainly on \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  (BI), especially following the recent comment that they have a mix of policies in their toolbox to cope with the recent spike in inflationary pressures," said Gundy Cahyadi, economist at OCBC in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 But for other Asian central banks, the situation is not as dire as capital outflows and inflation remain manageable.\par \par \uc2 They are unlikely to immediately tighten broadly easy policy settings in response to the changing Fed outlook.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday kept its policy rate unchanged at 2.50 percent as expected, after a recent cut to support growth and curb capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia and South Korea were expected also to hold policy rates steady when their monetary policy committees meet on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Asian central banks are generally mercantilist and will pick a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher growth," said Sean Yokota, head of Asian strategy at SEB. "The pace (of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline) may be open to debate, but the direction is fine with them."\par \par \uc2 In Indonesia, however, Yokoto noted that inflation was likely to head above 8 percent by year-end. Even if that was not sustained, he said, interest rates at 6 percent and 5-year government bond yields at 6.7 percent were too low.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last month became the first Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike its benchmark rate since 2011, and was widely expected to follow with another 25-basis-point move to 6.25 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Countries that run current account deficits tend to be more vulnerable because of the pressure in the balance of payments. As a whole though, external liquidity risk in the region remains manageable at least for now," Cahyadi said.\par \par \uc2 BIG TOOL KIT\par \par \uc2 Beyond raising its benchmark rate, BI could also hike its overnight deposit facility rate (FASBI) after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated it would "strengthen its policy mix" at this week's meeting, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 BI has also hinted it could soon introduce measures like tradable term deposits and an auction market in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to stem the flow of foreign funds.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe Indonesia should also introduce macroprudential measures such as a holding period for exporters' profits to slow declining \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which dropped to a two-year low of $98.1 billion in June.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian policymakers were not alone in reviewing their full range of tools in the face of the biggest inflection point for investors since 2008.\par \par \uc2 India's regulators on Monday toughened rules for derivatives trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a bid to arrest the steep decline of the rupee, which fell to a record low against the dollar this week and is emerging Asia's worst performer this year.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sonali Desai in SINGAPORE, Kitiphong Thaichareon in BANGKOK, Christine Kim in SEOUL and Anuradha Raghu in KUALA LUMPUR; Editing by \uc2 Simon Cameron-Moore\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 EMERGING-CENTRAL BANKS/ | ABN | M | E | RBN | D | SNS | SNI | SI | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130710e97a000ei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
