\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2013\par 03:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par             Immediate Range     Larger Range \par USD/CNY     6.1400-6.1488       6.1270-6.1530 \par USD/TWD     30.140-30.340       30.000-30.380 \par USD/KRW     1,150-1,160         1,148-1,163.5 \par USD/SGD     1.2702-1.2800       1.2700-1.2805 \par USD/MYR     3.1820-3.2000       3.1500-3.2290 \par USD/THB     31.09-31.20         31.00-31.35 \par USD/PHP     43.20-43.54         43.00-43.89 \par USD/IDR     9,900-9,950         9,850-10,000 \par USD/INR     60.50-60.76         60.00-61.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation. The PBOC central parity rate is likely to stabilize around its current level and may thus anchor USD/CNY just below the psychological barrier of 6.1500. The dollar is firming up again, which could mean that USD/CNY will remain buoyant until the July U.S.-China Strategic Economic Dialogue draws closer. Chinese stocks, already under pressure due to banking sector woes, may hit another down draft on the U.S. revising its first-quarter GDP growth estimate significantly lower to 1.8% from 2.4%. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1400 (psychological support), then at 6.1270 (Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1210 (June 3 record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1488 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), before 6.1530 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to maintain its course toward the monthly Bollinger midline at 30.530, as the pair manages to stay within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel again despite a brief dip. The USD/TWD pair has been well-supported on dips below the Bollinger channel and will likely stay that way as the U.S. dollar has been firm of late, even with the U.S. revising its first-quarter GDP growth estimate significantly lower. Today's \uc2 Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision meeting is likely to be a non-event -- economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires expect no change to the benchmark rate. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.140 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.940 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.340 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.380 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- upside bias. USD/KRW stays inside the Bollinger uptrend channel thus retaining its bullish bias toward the psychological barrier at KRW1,160, despite opening lower Thursday at KRW1,152.5 versus Wednesday's close of KRW1,154.5. A Thursday close above KRW1,150 would keep the Bollinger uptrend channel intact. Greenback strength looks likely to continue as the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield remains elevated above 2.5% and dollar index turns higher overnight in spite of a downward revision to the U.S. 1Q GDP growth estimate. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,150 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,148 (base of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,160 (psychological resistance), then at 1,163.5 (Tuesday's 1-year high), before 1,170 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- upside bias. USD/SGD is still trending higher within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel and may soon hit the top of the channel at 1.2805. Unless the pair closes under 1.2702 Thursday, the upside bias will remain in play. The greenback holds its ground despite a downward revision to U.S. 1Q GDP growth estimate, a sign that the market still believes the Fed is going to taper the pace of monetary stimulus this year. The bounce in U.S. stocks overnight should prop up Singapore stocks, which may help to support the Sing dollar as well. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2702 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2600 (20-day Bollinger mid and psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2805 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2900 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- upside bias. USD/MYR is likely to rise above the psychological resistance of 3.2000 again as the greenback rallies broadly on continued fear of the Fed reducing the pace of asset purchases. USD/MYR may aim for the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.2290 next, unless the pair ends the day below 3.1850 -- the base of the uptrend channel. Wednesday's downward revision to the U.S. 1Q GDP growth estimate was brushed off as backward-looking data and thus had little impact on \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields and the dollar. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.1820 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.1800 (psychological support), before 3.1500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2000 (major psychological resistance), then at 3.2290 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- upside bias. USD/THB is back within the bullish zone now that the pair has risen above the weekly Ichimoku Cloud and the into the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel once again. The weekly channel now props the pair up at 31.09 and may guide the dollar up to the next big target which is the monthly Bollinger midline at 31.35. Persistently high \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield and the market expecting the Fed to cut back on asset purchases soon is helping to keep the dollar well-bid on dips. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.09 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.06 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud), before 31.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.20 (psychological resistance), then at 31.35 (monthly Bollinger midline), before 31.44 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/PHP has been flirting with the 200-week moving average at 43.54, and may rise over this key level again Thursday due to the dollar index rally overnight. A Friday close above 43.54 may lend a more bullish tone to the USD/PHP pair and send it toward major psychological barrier at 44.00 again. Expectations for the Fed to pull back on quantitative easing are unlikely to be altered by the downgrade to the official U.S. 1Q GDP growth estimate, as the market understands it to be backward-looking data. Thus, the greenback will likely keep its firm tone in the medium term. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.20 (psychological support), then at 43.00 (major psychological support), before 42.70 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 43.54 (200-week moving average), then at 43.89 (monthly Bollinger mid), before 44.00 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. Spot USD/IDR is likely to be remain capped by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 9,950 level but the USD/IDR NDF contracts are looking well-supported and could stage a bounce toward 10,500 again as the greenback retains its biddish tone. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield -- an indicator of dollar strength -- remains elevated above 2.50% in spite of Wednesday's downgrade to the official estimate for U.S. 1Q GDP growth. The rupiah however, does look slightly better in fundamental terms and may hold its ground after ratings company \uc2 Moody's\uc2  gave a nod of approval to the Indonesia government's reduction of fuel subsidies -- a source of the country's chronic current account deficit. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 9,900 (psychological support), then at 9,850 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,780 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,950 (suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), before 10,000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation with upside bias. The India rupee made a new all-time low of INR60.76 to the dollar after bursting through the INR60.00 barrier that \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  said last week it would defend. Market participants Wednesday were eager to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from weakening further -- the RBI is known to cave in easily due to India's lean foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. The RBI's failure to stem the rupee's slide suggests that the street will look for more weakness to come. The next target is likely the psychological barrier at INR61.00. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.50 (psychological support), then at 60.00 (major psychological support), before 59.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 60.76 (record high), then at 61.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 27-06-13 0117GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130627e96r00017\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
