\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2013\par 03:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par             Immediate Range     Larger Range \par USD/CNY     6.1400-6.1500       6.1270-6.1570 \par USD/TWD     30.120-30.320       30.000-30.380 \par USD/KRW     1,150-1,160         1,148-1,163.5 \par USD/SGD     1.2685-1.2700       1.2600-1.2781 \par USD/MYR     3.1800-3.2000       3.1500-3.2150 \par USD/THB     30.80-31.00         30.69-31.09 \par USD/PHP     43.00-43.54         42.70-43.89 \par USD/IDR     9,900-9,950         9,850-10,000 \par USD/INR     59.50-59.98         59.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. The yuan may recover some losses as relief is appearing in China markets after the PBOC on Tuesday reassured that liquidity issues are being addressed and that currently volatility in the interbank rates is temporary. Interbank funding costs have eased from their recent highs but are still not back to the average before June. The PBOC central parity rate could keep the yuan roughly stable in line with the dollar index and USD/JPY. Stocks are likely to be choppy still but may have an upside bias due to market chatter that government agencies have been buying equities to prop up the market; this will boost equity investors' confidence. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1400 (psychological support), then at 6.1270 (Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1210 (June 3 record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1500 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1570 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. USD/TWD could ease off its week-highs and may consolidate near the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel. The direction of the pair may depend on movements in the Chinese yuan, which has been dominating North Asian markets this week. If the yuan strengthens, the Taiwan dollar is likely to follow as a proxy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . More downside potential may emerge for the USD/TWD pair if the greenback ends the day below 30.120 -- the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel. Thursday's Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision meeting is likely to be a non-event -- economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires expect no change to the benchmark rate. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.120 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.930 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.320 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.380 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/KRW gaps lower Wednesday following the pickup in risk sentiment overnight, but may consolidate ahead of the psychological support at 1,150. The massive bounce in China stocks late Tuesday and better-than-expected U.S. data overnight will help South Korea stocks to rally today and will benefit the won as well. The recovery of the won may be hampered by rising \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields, which are a bullish-USD indicator. The USD/KRW pair is hence likely to consolidate slightly lower between a 1,150-1,160 range. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,150 (psychological support), then at 1,148 (base of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,145 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,160 (psychological resistance), then at 1,163.5 (Tuesday's 1-year high), before 1,170 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- consolidation. USD/SGD corrected lower overnight on improved risk sentiment in the U.S. after strong economic data, which helped Wall Street to gain, but may consolidate near current levels. The USD/SGD pair has touched the bottom of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1.2685 where it may stall for now. Unless the pair ends Wednesday below 1.2685, more upside looks likely in the near term. The greenback could retain a bullish bias in the mid-term due to the elevated U.S. 10-year Treasury yield. Strong U.S. consumer confidence data and home sales data released Tuesday helped U.S. stocks to rally. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2685 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological support), before 1.2589 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1.2700 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2781 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- consolidation lower. USD/MYR may slip a little more toward the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1720 before consolidating. The steep USD/MYR selloff late Tuesday, triggered by the sharp recovery in China stocks, reveals the speculative market may have already been positioned long-USD -- hence the pair fell quickly due to a lack of fresh buyers. The next target for the greenback -- if the Bollinger uptrend is broken by the end of the day -- is likely the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 3.1290. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.1800 (psychological support), then at 3.1720 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2000 (major psychological resistance), then at 3.2150 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2200 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation lower. USD/THB continues to ease off its recent highs and is likely to consolidate between 30.80-31.00 in the near term. The USD/THB pair may however trend higher in the mid-term as long as the dollar remains within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which currently bottoms out at 30.69. Thai equities are likely to get a boost from the Tuesday rally in U.S. stocks on better-than-expected economic data, and also from the proposed buyout of \uc2 Bank of Ayudhya\uc2  by Japan's MUFG, which is helping to bolster Thai investor confidence. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.80 (psychological support), before 30.69 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 31.00 (psychological resistance), then at 31.06 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud), before 31.09 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- pullback lower. USD/PHP has broken below the 200-week moving average at 43.54 as risk appetite returns. The peso has come under immense pressure due to the emerging market selloff and may hence be primed for a relief rally toward the psychological support at 43.00. If the USD/PHP pair ends the week below 43.54, some upside pressure will ease. Upbeat U.S. economic data released Tuesday sent U.S. stocks higher overnight and may have a knock-on effect in Asia that could help the Manila stock market recover from its steep losses this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.70 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 43.54 (200-week moving average), then at 43.89 (monthly Bollinger mid), before 44.00 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. Spot USD/IDR may slip closer toward the 9,900 psychological level as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recover slightly on improving risk sentiment. The topside is likely to be remain capped by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 9,950 level. The USD/IDR NDF could dip as the rally appears to be running out steam, though the major support at 10,000 is likely to hold for now, especially with the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield -- an indicator of dollar strength -- remaining elevated above 2.50%. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  approval of the Indonesia government's reduction in fuel subsidies is seen as a positive for the country's current account deficit and therefore the rupiah. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 9,900 (psychological support), then at 9,850 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,780 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,950 (suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), before 10,000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation lower. USD/INR could fall back down toward the psychological support at 59.00 as the \uc2 Indian government\uc2  takes more steps to increase foreign direct investment. A revamped foreign direct investment policy that seeks to attract more overseas capital in the economy will be unveiled by the third week of July, said Finance Minister Chidambaram on Tuesday. The rupee is also likely to get a boost from the recovery in global risk sentiment, spurred by the Chinese authorities reassuring markets that the interbank funding issue is under control and the overnight rally in U.S. stocks on much better-than-expected economic data. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.50 (psychological support), then at 59.00 (psychological support), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 59.98 (record high), then at 60.00 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2013 21:01 ET (01:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130626e96q00013\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
