\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2013\par 02:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par             Immediate Range     Larger Range \par USD/CNY     6.1400-6.1500       6.1270-6.1612 \par USD/TWD     30.110-30.300       30.000-30.380 \par USD/KRW     1,150-1,160         1,148-1,170 \par USD/SGD     1.2700-1.2785       1.2686-1.2800 \par USD/MYR     3.2000-3.2200       3.1800-3.2500 \par USD/THB     31.00-31.06         30.80-31.09 \par USD/PHP     43.54-43.89         43.00-44.17 \par USD/IDR     9,900-9,930         9,830-10,000 \par USD/INR     59.50-59.98         59.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation lower. Tuesday's dollar/yuan parity rate might be set slightly lower in line with the slippage in USD/JPY. The fixing is likely to fall back below the CNY6.1800 psychological level and thus pressure spot USD/CNY down as well. The steep selloff in Chinese stocks Monday, which sent the Shanghai Composite index to a six-month low, may continue, and that would weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the more astute traders are still looking ahead to the July 8-12 China-U.S. Strategic Economic Dialogue, when analysts expect Beijing to announce new yuan liberalization moves. The PBOC may also also guide the yuan toward strength just ahead of the dialogue. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1400 (psychological support), then at 6.1270 (Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1210 (June 3 record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1511 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1612 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/TWD remains elevated within its Bollinger uptrend channel, but a pullback may come first as the pair has already hit the top of the channel at 30.300. The dollar is likely to hold on to its bullish bias as long as it stays above 30.110, which is the base of the uptrend channel, by the end of Tuesday. Better-than-expected industrial production figures released late Monday could also give the Taiwan dollar room to breathe. The industrial production data for May showed a contraction of 0.07% versus expectations for a 1.46% drop. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.110 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.920 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.300 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.380 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/KRW still appears to be very well-bid, though the pair is slightly overextended on the daily Bollinger band charts. The dollar broke a one-year high Monday after breaching the KRW1,160 psychological barrier, which may now serve as a resistance as the pair opens Tuesday lower at KRW1,159. A mild recovery in the Kospi, currently up 0.1%, appears to be underway and this may help the South Korean won to recoup some losses. However, the won will remain on a path toward weakness unless the USD/KRW pair ends Tuesday below KRW1,142 -- the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,150 (psychological support), then at 1,148 (base of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,142 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,160 (psychological resistance), before 1,170 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- consolidation lower. USD/SGD may slip down to 1.2686, which is the bottom of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The long-tailed doji candlestick Monday suggests upside momentum may be approaching exhaustion and thus the next move could be lower. The short-term uptrend bias, however, will remain intact so long as the pair ends the day above 1.2686. In order to nullify the bullish bias, USD/SGD needs to close below the uptrend channel, which could then hint at a move even lower to the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1.2589. The Sing dollar may have gotten a slight boost from Monday's higher-than-forecast CPI reading. Inflation rose 1.6% on year compared with estimates for a 1.2% increase. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  uses the Singapore dollar's relative strength to help control imported inflation, and thus may engineer a stronger Sing dollar by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2700 (psychological support), then at 1.2686 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2785 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- pullback lower. USD/MYR could reverse lower as the pair slips in tandem with its peer, the USD/SGD. The greenback may drop lower if the sell stoploss orders lurking below the 3.2000 psychological barrier are triggered; a fall to the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1750 may even be possible if the market is overly-skewed towards being long-USD. A sharp move lower could spook the weak holders of long-USD/MYR positions, who would then capitulate and sell the dollar. The external factor to watch for in these risk-sensitive markets may be Chinese stocks -- if another sharp fall occurs, the U.S. dollar could rise again. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.2000 (psychological support), then at 3.1800 (psychological support), before 3.1750 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2200 (psychological resistance), before 3.2500 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation lower. USD/THB appears to be coming off its recent highs and heading toward consolidation near the psychological support at 31.00. The baht is however likely to trend lower on a mid-term basis as long as the USD/THB pair remains within the Bollinger uptrend channel. The Bollinger uptrend channel base lies at 30.65. News of the proposed buyout of Bank Ayudhya by Japan's MUFG, which may not create much baht inflows since they will likely buy the 51% stake from other foreign investors, could help to bolster confidence in Thai stocks and therefore the baht. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 31.00 (psychological support), then at 30.80 (psychological support), before 30.65 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 31.06 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud), then at 31.09 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.36 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation lower. USD/PHP looks slightly heavy as the pair failed to stay above the psychological barrier of 44.00 and may thus take a peek at the downside in the short-term. The pair could drop back down to 43.54, which is the 200-week moving average support line as the greenback fades slightly across the board. However, mid-term weakness of the peso may continue unless the emerging market selloff abates. Investors, spooked by talk of the U.S. Federal Reserve pulling the plug on QE sooner-than-expected, have been liquidating risky emerging market debt and stocks, thus creating capital outflows that drag the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down as well. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.54 (200-week moving average), then at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.63 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 43.89 (monthly Bollinger mid), then at 44.00 (major psychological resistance), before 44.17 (Friday 1-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. Spot USD/IDR is likely to be remain capped by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 9,920-9,930 level, but could slip toward the psychological barrier at 9,900 as risk appetite stabilizes. The NDF market could dip as the topside move appears to be running out steam. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  approval of the Indonesia government's cutting of the fuel subsidy is seen as a positive for the country's current account deficit and therefore the rupiah. However, the underlying fear that the emerging market selloff could continue to batter Indonesia bonds and stocks may support the USD/IDR pair in the mid-term. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 9,900 (psychological support), then at 9,830 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,775 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,930 (suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), before 10,000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation. USD/INR appears to be supported still as the risk-off theme continues to play on, but the pair will likely stay below the major psychological barrier at 60.00. The Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drew the line in the sand at 60.00 Friday, saying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend the rupee to ensure it does not weaken past that mark. This will deter the speculative dollar-bulls and may even encourage short-selling of the dollar near the 60.00 mark -- that is, if the market believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is capable of defending that level with its limited foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.50 (psychological support), then at 59.00 (psychological support), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 59.98 (record high), then at 60.00 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 25-06-13 0045GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130625e96p0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
