\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2013\par 02:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par             Immediate Range     Larger Range \par USD/CNY     6.1270-6.1500       6.1210-6.1522 \par USD/TWD     30.100-30.280       30.000-30.340 \par USD/KRW     1,150-1,160         1,148-1,170 \par USD/SGD     1.2700-1.2779       1.2684-1.2800 \par USD/MYR     3.2000-3.2200       3.1800-3.2500 \par USD/THB     31.09-31.32         31.06-31.35 \par USD/PHP     43.56-43.89         43.00-44.17 \par USD/IDR     9,900-9,930         9,830-10,000 \par USD/INR     59.00-59.98         58.50-60.00 \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. The market is expecting a slightly weaker yuan parity rate Monday on the back of a rising U.S. dollar index and a weaker Japanese yen. The daily parity rate could be set around CNY6.1780-CNY6.1800, but spot USD/CNY could fall slightly as risk aversion appears to have moderated over the weekend. The USD/CNY pair could drop back inside the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at CNY6.1270. The PBOC injecting more liquidity into the market on Friday to tamp down rising short-term interest rates helped calm investors' nerves, which ought to help the Chinese equity markets to recover. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1270 (Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), before 6.1200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1522 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. The Taiwan dollar could regain lost ground Monday as the risk-off sentiment appears to be fading slightly, after an article by The Wall Street Journal's Jon Hilsenrath pointing out that the market may have misread the U.S. Federal Reserve's dovish cues. USD/TWD could hence drop to the psychological support at 30.000 as long-USD positions capitulate. If the USD/TWD pair ends the day below the 20-day Bollinger mid at 29.910, a mildly bearish signal would appear. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.100 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.910 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.280 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.340 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation lower. USD/KRW may slide toward the psychological support at 1,150 as risk appetite may improve following the 1.4% rally in the Nikkei Monday and the recovery of U.S. stocks on Friday. As risk appetite improves cautiously, the dollar could slide back down due to profit taking. The South Korea won dropped 2.4% last week, certainly enough for the short-term speculative players to buy the won in order to lock in some gains. USD/KRW could nullify the mid-term uptrend bias if it drops below the base of the monthly Bollinger uptrend channel at 1,148 by this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,150 (psychological support), then at 1,148 (base of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,140 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,160 (psychological resistance), before 1,170 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation lower. USD/SGD could correct lower toward the bottom of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1.2684 as risk appetite is expected to improve. The local equity market is expected to recover following the late-reversal in U.S. stocks Friday, possibly due to the dovish article by Jon Hilsenrath of The Wall Street Journal suggesting the Fed was misread by the market after FOMC, which ought to help soothe investors' fears of a mass selloff in stocks absent QE. The greenback could hence retreat as risk-off bets get pared, and may take on a more bearish bias if its ends the day below 1.2684 and therefore out of the uptrend channel. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2700 (psychological support), then at 1.2684 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2779 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2800 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--pullback lower. USD/MYR could reverse lower as the dollar may slip on profit-taking and a cautious return of risk appetite. The pair could break the major psychological barrier at 3.2000 and fall to the bottom of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1600 before consolidating. The change in sentiment comes as some traders react to the article by Jon Hilsenrath of The Wall Street Journal, which suggests the market has misread the Fed as being overly hawkish. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.2000 (psychological support), then at 3.1800 (psychological support), before 3.1600 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2200 (psychological resistance), before 3.2500 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation lower. USD/THB may consolidate at a slightly lower level toward the psychological support at 31.00 as risk appetite could improve slightly. The overnight rebound in U.S. stocks Friday and the dovish article by Jon Hilsenrath of The Wall Street Journal could help to mitigate fears of a market crash when the Fed tapers off the pace of quantitative easing. USD/THB is still in a mid-term uptrend bias unless the pair ends this week below 31.06 and therefore breaks the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.09 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.06 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud), before 31.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 31.32 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.35 (monthly Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation lower. USD/PHP may retreat further after the selloff Friday pressured the pair back under the psychological barrier of 44.00. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the Philippine peso, said one offshore NDF trader. The dollar may pullback against the peso due to profit-taking of long-USD positions and a slight improvement in risk appetite on the back of the Friday recovery of U.S. stocks and the dovish article by Jon Hilsenrath of The Wall Street Journal. However, the mid-term upside bias may persist if the USD/PHP pair stays above the 200-week moving average at 43.56. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.56 (200-week moving average), then at 43.00 (psychological support), before 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 43.89 (monthly Bollinger mid), then at 44.00 (major psychological resistance), before 44.17 (Friday 1-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation. Spot USD/IDR is likely to be remain capped by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 9,920-9,930 level, but could slip toward the psychological barrier at 9,900 as risk appetite stabilizes. The NDF market could dip as the topside move appears to be running out steam. Dollar bulls may also trim long-USD positions on the back of the dovish piece by the WSJ's Hilsenrath suggesting the market has misread the Fed as being overly hawkish. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 9,900 (psychological support), then at 9,830 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,775 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,930 (suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), before 10,000 (major psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--pullback lower. USD/INR is likely to retreat further away from the all-time high of 59.98 seen last Thursday and could possibly drop back below the psychological barrier at 59.00. The India \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 , drew the line in the sand at 60.00 Friday. The RBI official said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend the rupee to ensure it does not weaken past 60.00 to the U.S. dollar. This ought to spur profit-taking by those who have been shorting the rupee in expectation of more weakness. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.00 (psychological support), then at 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 59.98 (record high), then at 60.00 (major psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 23, 2013 20:51 ET (00:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130624e96o00066\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley