\par\par \b \uc2 DJ EWEN CHEW: USD/IDR soars to new 4-year high in NDF market as \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  caps spot...\b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2013\par 04:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The one-month USD/IDR contract hit a new four-year high of IDR10,565 as traders bought the dollar in reaction the U.S. Federal Reserve suggesting a year-end tapering of quantitative easing. The spot market has been relatively stable, capped by suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Agent banks of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were said to have sold dollars around IDR9,925 earlier. With the spot market capped and onshore liquidity limited to clients who have genuine outflows to hedge for, the speculative crowd has turned to the non-regulated offshore NDF market to position for a stronger U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Spot USD/IDR is now IDR9,920, while the 1-month NDF contract is priced at IDR10,475.\par \par \uc2 (ewen.chew@dowjones.com @djfxtrader)\par \par \uc2 (Ewen Chew is an Asia-Pacific \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporter at Dow Jones Newswires. Previously, he was an Asia NDF trader for five years, focusing on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia and the Philippines.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 19, 2013 22:54 ET (02:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130620e96k000b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
